t specifies several authentication protocols based on the SHA-2 hash functions for the User-based Security Model (USM) for SNMPv3 defined in RFC 3414.  It obsoletes RFC 7630, in which the MIB MODULE-IDENTITY value was incorrectly specified.fadNamelJoel Jaegglidarea£gacronymcopsdfullx$ops - Operations and Management AreadnamexOperations and Management AreagauthorsÇ¢kaffiliationxSecunet Security NetworksdnameiJ. Merkle¢kaffiliationcBSIdnamejM. Lochterddatej’«hfilenamegrfc7860eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymfopsawgdfullx5opsawg - Operations and Management Area Working Groupdnamex,Operations and Management Area Working Groupdtypebwgbidjdoc-129683hkeywordsÑdSNMPcUSMdHMACeSHA-2kobsoletedByÄepagesopublicationDateW$#granking¥crfcd7860irfcNumber¥estateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnameqProposed Standarddslugbpsfstream¢dnamedIETFdslugdietfetitlexQHMAC-SHA-2 Authentication Protocols in User-Based Security Model (USM) for SNMPv3dtypecrfciupdatedByÄ∂habstractyÔThis document extends RFC 7182, which specifies a framework for (and specific examples of) Integrity Check Values (ICVs) for packets and messages using the generalized packet/message format specified in RFC 5444.  It does so by defining an additional cryptographic function that allows the creation of an ICV that is an Identity-Based Signature (IBS), defined according to the Elliptic Curve-Based Certificateless Signatures for Identity-Based Encryption (ECCSI) algorithm specified in RFC 6507.fadNamemAlvaro Retanadarea£gacronymcrtgdfullrrtg - Routing AreadnamelRouting AreagauthorsÅ¢kaffiliationkBAE SystemsdnamekC. Dearloveddatej’»hfilenamegrfc7859eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymemanetdfullxmanet - Mobile Ad-hoc NetworksdnamevMobile Ad-hoc Networksdtypebwgbidjdoc-129682hkeywordsåx Mobile Ad hoc Networking (MANET)eMANETcTLVfOLSRv2uintegrity check valuecICVeECCSInelliptic curvexidentity-based signaturecIBSxidentity-based encryptioncIBEkobsoletedByÄepagesopublicationDateWF:ègranking≥crfcd7859irfcNumber≥estateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnamelExperimentaldslugcexpfstream¢dnamedIETFdslugdietfetitlexMIdentity-Based Signatures for Mobile Ad Hoc Network (MANET) Routing ProtocolsdtypecrfciupdatedByÄ∂habstractywThis document describes the use of Transport Layer Security (TLS) to provide privacy for DNS. Encryption provided by TLS eliminates opportunities for eavesdropping and on-path tampering with DNS queries in the network, such as discussed in RFC 7626. In addition, this document specifies two usage profiles for DNS over TLS and provides advice on performance considerations to minimize overhead from using TCP and TLS with DNS.

This document focuses on securing stub-to-recursive traffic, as per the charter of the DPRIVE Working Group. It does not prevent future applications of the protocol to recursive-to-authoritative traffic.fadNameoTerry Mandersondarea£gacronymcintdfullsint - Internet AreadnamemInternet AreagauthorsÜ¢kaffiliationgUSC/ISIdnameeZ. Hu¢kaffiliationgUSC/ISIdnamefL. Zhu¢kaffiliationgUSC/ISIdnamelJ. Heidemann¢kaffiliationkIndependentdnameiA. Mankin¢kaffiliationmVerisign LabsdnamejD. Wessels¢kaffiliationeICANNdnamejP. Hoffmanddatej’∆hfilenamegrfc7858eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedıegroup§gacronymfdprivedfullxdprive - DNS PRIVate ExchangednametDNS PRIVate Exchangedtypebwgbidjdoc-129681hkeywordsÇnDNS encryptionkDNS privacykobsoletedByÄepagesopublicationDateW;öágranking≤crfcd7858irfcNumber≤estateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnameqProposed Standarddslugbpsfstream¢dnamedIETFdslugdietfetitlex9Specification for DNS over Transport Layer Security (TLS)dtypecrfciupdatedByÅd8310∑habstractyThis document clarifies and updates several requirements of RFCs 4787, 5382, and 5508 based on operational and development experience. The focus of this document is Network Address Translation from IPv4 to IPv4 (NAT44).

