$The ability for a node to specify a forwarding path, other than the normal shortest path, that a particular packet will traverse, benefits a number of network functions. Source-based routing mechanisms have previously been specified for network protocols but have not seen widespread adoption. In this context, the term "source" means "the point at which the explicit route is imposed"; therefore, it is not limited to the originator of the packet (i.e., the node imposing the explicit route may be the ingress node of an operator's network).

This document outlines various use cases, with their requirements, that need to be taken into account by the Source Packet Routing in Networking (SPRING) architecture for unicast traffic. Multicast use cases and requirements are out of scope for this document.fadNamemAlvaro Retanadarea£gacronymcrtgdfullrrtg - Routing AreadnamelRouting AreagauthorsÜ¢kaffiliationsCisco Systems, Inc.dnamejS. Previdi¢kaffiliationsCisco Systems, Inc.dnamekC. Filsfils¢kaffiliationfOrangednamekB. Decraene¢kaffiliationfOrangednamelS. Litkowski¢kaffiliationpDeutsche TelekomdnamelM. Horneffer¢kaffiliationxJive Communications, Inc.dnameiR. Shakirddatejœ.hfilenamegrfc7855eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymfspringdfullx,spring - Source Packet Routing in Networkingdnamex#Source Packet Routing in Networkingdtypebwgbidjdoc-129678hkeywordsÄkobsoletedByÄepagesopublicationDateWF:ÜgrankingØcrfcd7855irfcNumberØestateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnamemInformationaldslugcinffstream¢dnamedIETFdslugdietfetitlexOSource Packet Routing in Networking (SPRING) Problem Statement and RequirementsdtypecrfciupdatedByÄ∂habstractyºThis document defines the BGP Monitoring Protocol (BMP), which can be used to monitor BGP sessions.  BMP is intended to provide a convenient interface for obtaining route views.  Prior to the introduction of BMP, screen scraping was the most commonly used approach to obtaining such views.  The design goals are to keep BMP simple, useful, easily implemented, and minimally service affecting.  BMP is not suitable for use as a routing protocol.fadNamelJoel Jaegglidarea£gacronymcopsdfullx$ops - Operations and Management AreadnamexOperations and Management AreagauthorsÉ¢kaffiliationpJuniper NetworksdnamejJ. Scudder¢kaffiliationmCisco SystemsdnamekR. Fernando¢kaffiliationfGooglednameiS. Stuartddatej’»hfilenamegrfc7854eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedıegroup§gacronymdgrowdfullx grow - Global Routing OperationsdnamexGlobal Routing Operationsdtypebwgbidjdoc-129677hkey