The mechanisms permit the data to be conveyed by reference (as an external resource) or by value (within the body of a SIP message or a location object). This follows the tradition of prior emergency services standardization work where data can be conveyed by value within the call signaling (i.e., in the body of the SIP message) or by reference.fadNamemAlissa Cooperdarea£gacronymcartdfullx%art - Applications and Real-Time AreadnamexApplications and Real-Time AreagauthorsÖ¢kaffiliation`dnamejR. Gellens¢kaffiliationgNeustardnamehB. Rosen¢kaffiliation`dnamemH. Tschofenig¢kaffiliationxTeleCommunication Systems, Inc.dnamekR. Marshall¢kaffiliationxWinterb Consulting ServicesdnameoJ. Winterbottomddatej’≤hfilenamegrfc7852eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymeecritdfullx?ecrit - Emergency Context Resolution with Internet Technologiesdnamex7Emergency Context Resolution with Internet Technologiesdtypebwgbidjdoc-129675hkeywordsÉtAdditional Call DatarEmergency ServicespCall InformationkobsoletedByÄepagesqopublicationDateWú8~granking¨crfcd7852irfcNumber¨estateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnameqProposed Standarddslugbpsfstream¢dnamedIETFdslugdietfetitlex,Additional Data Related to an Emergency CalldtypecrfciupdatedByÄ∂habstracty⁄This document describes mechanisms for Peer-to-Peer (P2P) overlay diagnostics.  It defines extensions to the REsource LOcation And Discovery (RELOAD) base protocol to collect diagnostic information and details the protocol specifications for these extensions.  Useful diagnostic information for connection and node status monitoring is also defined.  The document also describes the usage scenarios and provides examples of how these methods are used to perform diagnostics.fadNamemAlissa Cooperdarea£gacronymcartdfullx%art - Applications and Real-Time AreadnamexApplications and Real-Time AreagauthorsÖ¢kaffiliationfHuaweidnamegH. Song¢kaffiliationfHuaweidnamehX. Jiang¢kaffiliationfHuaweidnamegR. Even¢kaffiliationlethernot.orgdnamehD. Bryan