dByÄ∂habstractyyHTTP Origin-Bound Authentication (HOBA) is a digital-signature-based design for an HTTP authentication method.  The design can also be used in JavaScript-based authentication embedded in HTML.  HOBA is an alternative to HTTP authentication schemes that require passwords and therefore avoids all problems related to passwords, such as leakage of server-side password databases.fadNameqKathleen Moriartydarea£gacronymcsecdfullssec - Security AreadnamemSecurity AreagauthorsÉ¢kaffiliationvTrinity College DublindnamejS. Farrell¢kaffiliationnVPN ConsortiumdnamejP. Hoffman¢kaffiliationiPhresheezdnameiM. Thomasddatej’Öhfilenamegrfc7486eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymhhttpauthdfullx5httpauth - Hypertext Transfer Protocol Authenticationdnamex*Hypertext Transfer Protocol Authenticationdtypebwgbidjdoc-129311hkeywordsÉuNetwork Working Groupshttp authenticationporigin-bound keykobsoletedByÄepagesopublicationDateTˇì^granking>crfcd7486irfcNumber>estateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnamelExperimentaldslugcexpfstream¢dnamedIETFdslugdietfetitlex'HTTP Origin-Bound Authentication (HOBA)dtypecrfciupdatedByÄ∂habstracty¨WHOIS output objects from registries, including both Regional Internet Registries (RIRs) and Domain Name Registries (DNRs), were collected and analyzed.  This document describes the process and results of the statistical analysis of existing WHOIS information.  The purpose of this document is to build an object inventory to facilitate discussions of data objects included in Registration Data Access Protocol (RDAP) responses.fadNamelPete Resnickdarea£gacronymcappdfullwapp - Applications AreadnameqApplications AreagauthorsÖ¢kaffiliationeCNNICdnamegL. Zhou¢kaffiliationeCNNICdnamegN. Kong¢kaffiliationeCNNICdnamegS. Shen¢kaffiliationeICANNdnamehS. Sheng¢kaffiliationfLACNICdnameiA. Servinddatej’zhfilenamegrfc7485eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymfweirdsdfullx:weirds - Web Extensible Internet Registration Data Serviced