PdATPScVBRnAuthenticationjReputationkobsoletedByÅd7601epages+opublicationDateR<®}grankingYcrfcd7001irfcNumberYestateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnameqProposed Standarddslugbpsfstream¢dnamedIETFdslugdietfetitlexAMessage Header Field for Indicating Message Authentication StatusdtypecrfciupdatedByÅd7410∂habstracty>This document specifies a mechanism that enables a Routing Protocol for Low-power and Lossy Networks (RPL) router to measure the aggregated values of given routing metrics along an existing route towards another RPL router, thereby allowing the router to decide if it wants to initiate the discovery of a better route.fadNamemAdrian Farreldarea£gacronymcrtgdfullrrtg - Routing AreadnamelRouting AreagauthorsÑ¢kaffiliationx!University of Wisconsin MilwaukeednamehM. Goyal¢kaffiliationeINRIAdnamekE. Baccelli¢kaffiliationmSigma DesignsdnameiA. Brandt¢kaffiliationpJohnson ControlsdnamekJ. Martocciddatej’+hfilenamegrfc6998eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymdrolldfullx0roll - Routing Over Low power and Lossy networksdnamex)Routing Over Low power and Lossy networksdtypebwgbidjdoc-128831hkeywordsÖkMeasurementmRoute QualityjP2P RoutescRPLdROLLkobsoletedByÄepagesopublicationDateR∞ggrankingVcrfcd6998irfcNumberVestateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnamelExperimentaldslugcexpfstream¢dnamedIETFdslugdietfetitlexhA Mechanism to Measure the Routing Metrics along a Point-to-Point Route in a Low-Power and Lossy NetworkdtypecrfciupdatedByÄ∂habstractypThis document specifies a point-to-point route discovery mechanism, complementary to the Routing Protocol for Low-power and Lossy Networks (RPL) core functionality.  This mechanism allows an IPv6 router to discover "on demand" routes to one or more IPv6 routers in a Low-power and Lossy Network (LLN) such that the discovered routes meet specified metrics constraints.fadNamemAdrian Farreldarea£gacronymcrtgdfullrrtg - Routing AreadnamelRouting AreagauthorsÖ¢kaffiliationx!University of Wisconsin MilwaukeednamehM. Goyal¢kaf