new TCP options that use these codepoints.fadNamerMartin Stiemerlingdarea£gacronymcwitdfullx wit - Web and Internet TransportdnamexWeb and Internet TransportgauthorsÅ¢kaffiliationgUSC/ISIdnamehJ. TouchddatejŒ>hfilenamegrfc6994eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymdtcpmdfullx+tcpm - TCP Maintenance and Minor Extensionsdnamex$TCP Maintenance and Minor Extensionsdtypebwgbidjdoc-128828hkeywordsÄkobsoletedByÄepagesopublicationDateRÚmgrankingRcrfcd6994irfcNumberRestateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnameqProposed Standarddslugbpsfstream¢dnamedIETFdslugdietfetitlex&Shared Use of Experimental TCP OptionsdtypecrfciupdatedByÄ∂habstractx“This document defines and registers a value of "impp" ("instant messaging and presence protocol") for the "purpose" header field parameter of the Call-Info header field in the Session Initiation Protocol (SIP).fadNameqGonzalo Camarillodarea£gacronymcgendfullrgen - General AreadnamelGeneral AreagauthorsÅ¢kaffiliationsCisco Systems, Inc.dnamenP. Saint-Andreddatej’5hfilenamegrfc6993eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymdnonedfullxnone - Individual SubmissionsdnamevIndividual Submissionsdtypegindividbidjdoc-128827hkeywordsÖcSIPiCall-Infolheader fieldqInstant MessaginghPresencekobsoletedByÄepagesopublicationDateQˆ°1grankingQcrfcd6993irfcNumberQestateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnamemInformationaldslugcinffstream¢dnamedIETFdslugdietfetitlexnInstant Messaging and Presence Purpose for the Call-Info Header Field in the Session Initiation Protocol (SIP)dtypecrfciupdatedByÄ∂habstractx˜This document describes a routing scenario where IPv4 packets are transported over an IPv6 network, based on the methods described in RFCs 6145 and 6052, along with a separate OSPFv3 routing table for IPv4-embedded IPv6 routes in the IPv6 network.fadNamenStewart Bryantdarea£gacronymcrtgdfullrrtg - Routing AreadnamelRouting AreagauthorsÉ¢kaffiliationsHuawei TechnologiesdnamehD. Cheng¢kaffiliationnFrance TelecomdnamelM. Boucadair¢kaffiliati