ryptographic authentication algorithm in addition to the already-documented authentication schemes, described in the base specification and RFC 5304. IS-IS is specified in International Standards Organization (ISO) 10589, with extensions to support Internet Protocol version 4 (IPv4) described in RFC 1195.

Although this document has been written specifically for using the Hashed Message Authentication Code (HMAC) construct along with the Secure Hash Algorithm (SHA) family of cryptographic hash functions, the method described in this document is generic and can be used to extend IS-IS to support any cryptographic hash function in the future. [STANDARDS-TRACK]fadNamekRoss Callondarea£gacronymcrtgdfullrrtg - Routing AreadnamelRouting AreagauthorsÜ¢kaffiliationnAlcatel-LucentdnameiM. Bhatia¢kaffiliationkIP InfusiondnameiV. Manral¢kaffiliationuRedback Networks Inc.dnameeT. Li¢kaffiliationpExtreme NetworksdnamekR. Atkinson¢kaffiliationmCisco SystemsdnamehR. White¢kaffiliationsAegis Data SecuritydnamehM. Fantoddatej‘=hfilenamegrfc5310eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedıegroup§gacronymdisisdfullxisis - IS-IS for IP InternetsdnamevIS-IS for IP Internetsdtypebwgbidjdoc-127204hkeywordsÑeIS-IShSecurityhHMAC-SHAxCryptographic AuthenticationkobsoletedByÄepagesopublicationDateIê«grankingæcrfcd5310irfcNumberæestateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnameqProposed Standarddslugbpsfstream¢dnamedIETFdslugdietfetitlex*IS-IS Generic Cryptographic AuthenticationdtypecrfciupdatedByÇd6232d6233∂habstracty”The two predominant circuit types used by link state routing protocols are point-to-point and broadcast.  It is important to identify the correct circuit type when forming adjacencies, flooding link state database packets, and representing the circuit topologically.  This document describes a simple mechanism to treat the broadcast network as a point-to-point connection from the standpoint of IP routing.  This memo provides information for the Internet community.fadNamekBill Fennerdarea£gacronymcrtgdfullrrtg - Routing AreadnamelRouting AreagauthorsÇ¢kaffiliationmCisco SystemsdnamegN. Shen¢kaffiliationnAlcatel-LucentdnamehA. Zininddatej—Ahfilenamegrfc5309eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymdisisdfullxisis - IS-IS for IP InternetsdnamevIS-IS for IP Internetsdtypebwgbi