This memo obsoletes RFC 1850; however, it is designed to be backwards compatible. The functional differences between this memo and RFC 1850 are explained in Appendix B. [STANDARDS-TRACK]fadNamekBill Fennerdarea£gacronymcrtgdfullrrtg - Routing AreadnamelRouting AreagauthorsÉ¢kaffiliationfNorteldnamehD. Joyal¢kaffiliationgAirvanadnamejP. Galecki¢kaffiliationdCSFBdnamelS. Giacaloneddatej”≥hfilenamegrfc4750eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymdospfdfullx#ospf - Open Shortest Path First IGPdnamexOpen Shortest Path First IGPdtypebwgbidjdoc-126667hkeywordsáhOSPF-MIBxOpen Shortest Path FirstcSPFcMIBgroutingvnetwork management mibmOSPF-TRAP-MIBkobsoletedByÄepagesyopublicationDateEÄE#grankingécrfcd4750irfcNumberéestateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnameqProposed Standarddslugbpsfstream¢dnamedIETFdslugdietfetitlex*OSPF Version 2 Management Information BasedtypecrfciupdatedByÄ∂habstractxÛThis document specifies a Real-time Transport Protocol (RTP) payload format to be used for the International Telecommunication Union (ITU-T) G.729.1 audio codec.  A media type registration is included for this payload format. [STANDARDS-TRACK]fadNamevCullen Fluffy Jenningsdarea£gacronymcraidfullx4rai - Real-time Applications and Infrastructure Areadnamex.Real-time Applications and Infrastructure AreagauthorsÅ¢kaffiliationnFrance TelecomdnamejA. Sollaudddatej”¿hfilenamegrfc4749eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedıegroup§gacronymcavtdfullxavt - Audio/Video TransportdnameuAudio/Video Transportdtypebwgbidjdoc-126666hkeywordsÉxreal-time transport protocoleitu-tx%international telecommunication unionkobsoletedByÄepagesopublicationDateE@<grankingçcrfcd4749irfcNumberçestateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnameqProposed Standarddslugbpsfstream¢dnamedIETFdslugdietfetitlex.RTP Payload Format for the G.729.1 Audio CodecdtypecrfciupdatedByÅd5459∂habstractyäThis document updates RFC 3978 "IETF Rights in Contributions" to recognize that the IETF Trust is now the proper custodian of all 