This document discusses the involved network entities and the relationship between IKEv2 signaling and information provided by other protocols. Design decisions for the MOBIKE protocol, background information, and discussions within the working group are recorded. This memo provides information for the Internet community.fadNamelRuss Housleydarea£gacronymcsecdfullssec - Security AreadnamemSecurity AreagauthorsÇ¢kaffiliationmSafenet, Inc.dnamejT. Kivinen¢kaffiliationgSiemensdnamemH. Tschofenigddatej”¨hfilenamegrfc4621eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymfmobikedfullx'mobike - IKEv2 Mobility and MultihomingdnamexIKEv2 Mobility and Multihomingdtypebwgbidjdoc-126542hkeywordsÅuinternet key exchangekobsoletedByÄepagesopublicationDateD⁄Åπgrankingcrfcd4621irfcNumberestateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnamemInformationaldslugcinffstream¢dnamedIETFdslugdietfetitlex>Design of the IKEv2 Mobility and Multihoming (MOBIKE) ProtocoldtypecrfciupdatedByÄ∂habstractyÆThis document describes a protocol for asking an IPv6 node to supply certain network information, such as its hostname or fully-qualified domain name.  IPv6 implementation experience has shown that direct queries for a hostname are useful, and a direct query mechanism for other information has been found useful in serverless environments and for debugging.  This memo defines an Experimental Protocol for the Internet community.fadNameoMargaret Cullendarea£gacronymcintdfullsint - Internet AreadnamemInternet AreagauthorsÇ¢kaffiliationhFermilabdnamekM. Crawford¢kaffiliationgJHU APLdnamekB. Habermanddatej”ùhfilenamegrfc4620eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymdipv6dfullx!ipv6 - IP Version 6 Working GroupdnamexIP Version 6 Working Groupdtypebwgbidjdoc-126541hkeywordsÅxinternet protocol version 6kobsoletedByÄepagesopublicationDateD⁄Å¡grankingcrfcd4620irfcNumberestateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnamelExperimentaldslugcexpfstream¢dnamedIETFdslugdietfetitlexIPv6 Node Information QueriesdtypecrfciupdatedByÄ∂habstractyOA frame relay pseudowire is a mechanism that exists between a provider's edge network nodes and that supports as faithfully as possible frame relay services over an MPLS packet switched network (PSN).  This document describes the detailed encapsulation necessary to transport frame relay packets over an MPLS network. [STANDARDS-TRACK]fadNamemMark Townsleydarea£gacronymcrtgdfullrrtg - Routing AreadnamelRouting AreagauthorsÉ¢kaffiliationsCisco Systems, Inc.dnamejL. Martini¢kaffiliationqOz CommunicationsdnamegC. Kawa¢kaffiliationgTellabsdnamehA. Malisddatej”ßhfilenamegrfc4619eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymdpwe3dfullx(pwe3 - Pseudowire Emulation Edge to Edgednamex!Pseudowire Emulation Edge to Edgedtypebwgbidjdoc-126540hkeywordsÑjpseudowirecpsnwpacket switched networkbpwkobsoletedByÄepagesopublicationDateE‡∂grankingcrfcd4619irfcNumberestateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnameqProposed Standarddslugbpsfstream¢dnamedIETFdslugdietfetitlexeEncapsulation Methods for Transport of Frame Relay over Multiprotocol Label Switching (MPLS) NetworksdtypecrfciupdatedByÄ∂habstracty¡A pseudowire (PW) can be used to carry Point to Point Protocol (PPP) or High-Level Data Link Control (HDLC) Protocol Data Units over a Multiprotocol Label Switching (MPLS) network without terminating the PPP/HDLC protocol.  This enables service providers to offer "emulated" HDLC, or PPP link services over existing MPLS networks.  This document specifies the encapsulation of PPP/HDLC Packet Data Units (PDUs) within a pseudowire. [STANDARDS-TRACK]fadNamemMark Townsleydarea£gacronymcrtgdfullrrtg - Routing AreadnamelRouting AreagauthorsÑ¢kaffiliationsCisco Systems, Inc.dnamejL. Martini¢kaffiliationsCisco Systems, Inc.dnamehE. Rosen¢kaffiliationgTellabsdnamehG. Heron¢kaffiliationgTellabsdnamehA. Malisddatej”±hfilenamegrfc4618eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymdpwe3dfullx(pwe3 - Pseudowire Emulation Edge to Edgednamex!Pseudowire Emulation Edge to Edgedtypebwgbidjdoc-126539hkeywordsÖbpwjpseudowirewpoint to point protocolcpduppacket data unitkobsoletedByÄepagesopublicationDateE‡©granking
