tationkobsoletedByÄepagesopublicationDateB;Å◊grankingßcrfcd4007irfcNumberßestateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnameqProposed Standarddslugbpsfstream¢dnamedIETFdslugdietfetitlex IPv6 Scoped Address ArchitecturedtypecrfciupdatedByÇd9844d7346∂habstracty	This document specifies a Diameter application that can be used to implement real-time credit-control for a variety of end user services such as network access, Session Initiation Protocol (SIP) services, messaging services, and download services. [STANDARDS-TRACK]fadNamekBert Wijnendarea£gacronymcopsdfullx$ops - Operations and Management AreadnamexOperations and Management AreagauthorsÖ¢kaffiliationhEricssondnameiH. Hakala¢kaffiliationhEricssondnamejL. Mattila¢kaffiliationeNokiadnamemJ-P. Koskinen¢kaffiliationeNokiadnamehM. Stura¢kaffiliationeNokiadnamekJ. Loughneyddatej—Khfilenamegrfc4006eflags£mhiddenDefaultıiobsoletedıgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymcaaadfullx2aaa - Authentication, Authorization and Accountingdnamex,Authentication, Authorization and Accountingdtypebwgbidjdoc-125941hkeywordsÅxreal-time credit-controlkobsoletedByÅd8506epagesropublicationDateC˛êgranking¶crfcd4006irfcNumber¶estateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnameqProposed Standarddslugbpsfstream¢dnamedIETFdslugdietfetitlex#Diameter Credit-Control ApplicationdtypecrfciupdatedByÄ∂habstracty§This document describes the Diameter protocol application used for Authentication, Authorization, and Accounting (AAA) services in the Network Access Server (NAS) environment. When combined with the Diameter Base protocol, Transport Profile, and Extensible Authentication Protocol specifications, this application specification satisfies typical network access services requirements.

Initial deployments of the Diameter protocol are expected to include legacy systems. Therefore, this application has been carefully designed to ease the burden of protocol conversion between RADIUS and Diameter. This is achieved by including the RADIUS attribute space to eliminate the need to perform many attribute translations.

The interactions between Diameter applications and RADIUS specified in this document are to be applied to all Diameter applications. In this sense, this document extends the Base Diameter protocol. [STANDARDS-TRACK]fadNamekBert Wijnendarea£gacronymcopsdfullx$ops - Operations and Management AreadnamexOperations and Management AreagauthorsÑ¢kaffiliationrCisco Systems Inc.dnamejP. Calhoun¢kaffiliationrCisco Systems Inc.dnamegG. Zorn¢kaffiliationjConsultantdnameiD. Spence¢kaffiliationqCircular NetworksdnameiD. Mittonddatej—Ohfilenamegrfc4005eflags£mhiddenDefaultıiobsoletedıgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymcaaadfullx2aaa - Authentication, Authorization and Accountingdnamex,Authentication, Authorization and Accountingdtypebwgbidjdoc-125940hkeywordsácaaax'authentication authorization accountingcnasmdiameter baseqtransport profilex"extensible authentication protocolfradiuskobsoletedByÅd7155epagesUopublicationDateB˙èÉgranking•crfcd4005irfcNumber•estateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnameqProposed Standarddslugbpsfstream¢dnamedIETFdslugdietfetitlex*Diameter Network Access Server ApplicationdtypecrfciupdatedByÄ∂habstractyÈThis document specifies a Diameter application that allows a Diameter server to authenticate, authorize and collect accounting information for Mobile IPv4 services rendered to a mobile node.  Combined with the Inter-Realm capability of the base protocol, this application allows mobile nodes to receive service from foreign service providers.  Diameter Accounting messages will be used by the foreign and home agents to transfer usage information to the Diameter servers. [STANDARDS-TRACK]fadNamekBert Wijnendarea£gacronymcopsdfullx$ops - Operations and Management AreadnamexOperations and Management AreagauthorsÖ¢kaffiliationsCisco Systems, Inc.dnamejP. Calhoun¢kaffiliationnBytemobile IncdnamelT. Johansson¢kaffiliationuNokia Research CenterdnamejC. Perkins¢kaffiliationsLucent TechnologiesdnameiT. Hiller¢kaffiliationsLucent TechnologiesdnameiP. McCannddatej—Mhfilenamegrfc40