igrankingAcrfcd3649irfcNumberAestateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnamelExperimentaldslugcexpfstream¢dnamedIETFdslugdietfetitlex*HighSpeed TCP for Large Congestion WindowsdtypecrfciupdatedByÄ∂habstracty˙This specification extends the Web Distributed Authoring and Versioning (WebDAV) Protocol to support the server-side ordering of collection members.  Of particular interest are orderings that are not based on property values, and so cannot be achieved using a search protocol's ordering option and cannot be maintained automatically by the server.  Protocol elements are defined to let clients specify the position in the ordering of each collection member, as well as the semantics governing the ordering.fadNamejTed Hardiedarea£gacronymcappdfullwapp - Applications AreadnameqApplications AreagauthorsÇ¢kaffiliationoU.C. Santa CruzdnamelJ. Whitehead¢kaffiliationjgreenbytesdnamejJ. Reschkeddatej—›hfilenamegrfc3648eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymfwebdavdfullx1webdav - WWW Distributed Authoring and Versioningdnamex(WWW Distributed Authoring and Versioningdtypebwgbidjdoc-125596hkeywordsáfWebDAVx)Web Distribution Authoring and Versioningwserver client semanticshorderingqorderpatch methodoposition headertordering-type headerkobsoletedByÄepagesopublicationDate?ﬁS‰granking@crfcd3648irfcNumber@estateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnameqProposed Standarddslugbpsfstream¢dnamedIETFdslugdietfetitlexNWeb Distributed Authoring and Versioning (WebDAV) Ordered Collections ProtocoldtypecrfciupdatedByÄ∂habstracty	This document presents a framework to assist the writers of certificate policies or certification practice statements for participants within public key infrastructures, such as certification authorities, policy authorities, and communities of interest that wish to rely on certificates.  In particular, the framework provides a comprehensive list of topics that potentially (at the writer's discretion) need to be covered in a certificate policy or a certification practice statement.  This document supersedes RFC 2527.fadNamelRuss Housleydarea£gacronymcsecdfullssec - Security AreadnamemSecurity AreagauthorsÖ¢kaffiliationxOrion Security Solutions, Inc.dnamekS. Chokhani¢kaffiliationnVeriSign, Inc.dnamegW. Ford¢kaffiliationrCooley Godward LLPdnameiR. Sabett¢kaffiliationwMcCarter & English, LLPdnamejC. Merrill¢kaffiliationpInfoliance, Inc.dnameeS. Wuddatej“Óhfilenamegrfc3647eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymdpkixdfullx(pkix - Public-Key Infrastructure (X.509)dnamex!Public-Key Infrastructure (X.509)dtypebwgbidjdoc-125595hkeywordsÑdpkixjencryptionhsecuritynauthenticationkobsoletedByÄepages^opublicationDate?©K?granking?crfcd3647irfcNumber?estateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnamemInformationaldslugcinffstream¢dnamedIETFdslugdietfetitlexaInternet X.509 Public Key Infrastructure Certificate Policy and Certification Practices FrameworkdtypecrfciupdatedByÄ∂habstractx∂This document describes Dynamic Host Configuration Protocol for IPv6 (DHCPv6) options for passing a list of available DNS recursive name servers and a domain search list to a client.fadNameqDr. Thomas Nartendarea£gacronymcintdfullsint - Internet AreadnamemInternet AreagauthorsÅ¢kaffiliationmCisco SystemsdnamehR. Dromsddatej—›hfilenamegrfc3646eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymcdhcdfullx dhc - Dynamic Host ConfigurationdnamexDynamic Host Configurationdtypebwgbidjdoc-125594hkeywordsácDNSrdomain name systemgservicefserverfclientdDHCPx#Dynamic Host Configuration ProtocolkobsoletedByÄepagesopublicationDate?÷+␀granking>crfcd3646irfcNumber>estateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnameqProposed Standarddslugbpsfstream¢dnamedIETFdslugdietfetitlexSDNS Configuration options for Dynamic Host Configuration Protocol for IPv6 (DHCPv6)dtypecrfciupdatedByÄ∂habstractyRThe Secret Key Transaction Authentication for DNS (TSIG) protocol provides transaction level authentication for DNS.  TSIG is extensible through the definition of new algorithms.  This document 