fadNamejTed Hardiedarea£gacronymdiesgdfullx*iesg - Internet Engineering Steering Groupdnamex#Internet Engineering Steering GroupgauthorsÅ¢kaffiliationsAdacel TechnologiesdnamegS. Leggddatej”hfilenamegrfc3642eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymcappdfullwapp - Applications AreadnameqApplications Areadtypedareabidjdoc-125590hkeywordsÇeasn.1xabstract syntax notationkobsoletedByÄepagesopublicationDate?ï∏ïgranking:crfcd3642irfcNumber:estateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnamemInformationaldslugcinffstream¢dnamedIETFdslugdietfetitlexACommon Elements of Generic String Encoding Rules (GSER) EncodingsdtypecrfciupdatedByÄ∂habstractxŸThis document defines a set of Abstract Syntax Notation One (ASN.1) encoding rules, called the Generic String Encoding Rules (GSER), that produce a human readable text encoding for values of any given ASN.1 data type.fadNamejTed Hardiedarea£gacronymdiesgdfullx*iesg - Internet Engineering Steering Groupdnamex#Internet Engineering Steering GroupgauthorsÅ¢kaffiliationsAdacel TechnologiesdnamegS. Leggddatej”hfilenamegrfc3641eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedıegroup§gacronymcappdfullwapp - Applications AreadnameqApplications Areadtypedareabidjdoc-125589hkeywordsÇeasn.1xabstract syntax notationkobsoletedByÄepagesopublicationDate?ï∏Qgranking9crfcd3641irfcNumber9estateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnameqProposed Standarddslugbpsfstream¢dnamedIETFdslugdietfetitlex4Generic String Encoding Rules (GSER) for ASN.1 TypesdtypecrfciupdatedByÅd4792∂habstractymThe Motion Picture Experts Group (MPEG) Committee (ISO/IEC JTC1/SC29 WG11) is a working group in ISO that produced the MPEG-4 standard.  MPEG defines tools to compress content such as audio-visual information into elementary streams.  This specification defines a simple, but generic RTP payload format for transport of any non-multiplexed MPEG-4 elementary stream.fadNameqAllison J. Mankindarea£gacronymcraidfullx4rai - Real-time Applications and Infrastructure Areadnamex.Real-time Appli