document defines an extension to the Sieve mail filtering language that allows users to compare against the user and detail parts of an address. [STANDARDS-TRACK]fadNameiNed Freeddarea£gacronymdiesgdfullx*iesg - Internet Engineering Steering Groupdnamex#Internet Engineering Steering GroupgauthorsÅ¢kaffiliationrOceana Matrix Ltd.dnamelK. Murchisonddatej”8hfilenamegrfc3598eflags£mhiddenDefaultıiobsoletedıgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymcappdfullwapp - Applications AreadnameqApplications Areadtypedareabidjdoc-125548hkeywordsàeusersxdetailed addressing languagegaddressdpartdtestfdetailffiltergmailboxkobsoletedByÅd5233epagesopublicationDate?_[πgrankingcrfcd3598irfcNumberestateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnameqProposed Standarddslugbpsfstream¢dnamedIETFdslugdietfetitlex-Sieve Email Filtering -- Subaddress ExtensiondtypecrfciupdatedByÄ∂habstracty	Extending the Domain Name System (DNS) with new Resource Record (RR) types currently requires changes to name server software.  This document specifies the changes necessary to allow future DNS implementations to handle new RR types transparently. [STANDARDS-TRACK]fadNamekRalph Dromsdarea£gacronymcintdfullsint - Internet AreadnamemInternet AreagauthorsÅ¢kaffiliationlNominum Inc.dnamemA. Gustafssonddatej”8hfilenamegrfc3597eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedıegroup§gacronymfdnsextdfullwdnsext - DNS ExtensionsdnamenDNS Extensionsdtypebwgbidjdoc-125547hkeywordsácDNSrdomain name systemtname server softwarekcompressionltransparencybRRoResource RecordkobsoletedByÄepagesopublicationDate?_[Rgrankingcrfcd3597irfcNumberestateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnameqProposed Standarddslugbpsfstream¢dnamedIETFdslugdietfetitlex2Handling of Unknown DNS Resource Record (RR) TypesdtypecrfciupdatedByÜd4033d4034d4035d5395d6195d6895∑habstractyThis document defines the changes that need to be made to the Domain Name System (DNS) to support hosts running IP version 6 (IPv6).  The changes include a resource record type to store an IPv6 address, a domain to support lookups based on an IPv6 address, and updated definitions of existing query types that return Internet addresses as part of additional section processing.  The extensions are designed to be compatible with existing applications and, in particular, DNS implementations themselves. [STANDARDS-TRACK]fadNamemErik Nordmarkdarea£gacronymcintdfullsint - Internet AreadnamemInternet AreagauthorsÑ¢kaffiliationeCiscodnamejS. Thomson¢kaffiliationiMicrosoftdnamejC. Huitema¢kaffiliatione6WINDdnamejV. Ksinant¢kaffiliationeAFNICdnamejM. Souissiddatej”hfilenamegrfc3596eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymfdnsextdfullwdnsext - DNS ExtensionsdnamenDNS Extensionsdtypebwgbidjdoc-125546hkeywordsÑqinternet protocolrdomain name systemcDNSdzonekobsoletedByÄepagesopublicationDate?É?grankingcrfcd3596irfcNumberestateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnameqInternet Standarddslugcstdfstream¢dnamedIETFdslugdietfisubseries£gacronymcstdfnumberXetotaletitlex&DNS Extensions to Support IP Version 6dtypecrfciupdatedByÄ∂habstractyThis MIB module defines textual conventions to represent the commonly used IPv6 Flow Label.  The intent is that these textual conventions (TCs) will be imported and used in MIB modules that would otherwise define their own representations. [STANDARDS-TRACK]fadNamejRandy Bushdarea£gacronymcopsdfullx$ops - Operations and Management AreadnamexOperations and Management AreagauthorsÅ¢kaffiliationsLucent TechnologiesdnameiB. Wijnenddatej”8hfilenamegrfc3595eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymgopsareadfullx3opsarea - Operations & Management Area Open Meetingdnamex)Operations & Management Area Open Meetingdtypebagbidjdoc-125545hkeywordsÇcmibxmanagement information basekobsoletedByÄepagesopublicationDate?b/:grankingcrfcd3595irfcNumberestateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnameqProposed Standarddslugbpsfstream¢dnamedIETFdslugdietfetitlex'Textual Conventions for IPv6 Flow LabeldtypecrfciupdatedByÄ∂habstracty+This document defines a new sub-option for the DHCP CableLabs Client Configuration (CCC) Option.  This new sub-option will be used to direct CableLabs Client Devices (CCDs) to invalidate security tickets stored in CCD non volatile memory (i.e., locally persisted security tickets). [STANDARDS-TRACK]fadNameqDr. Thomas Nartendarea£gacronymcintdfullsint - Internet AreadnamemInternet AreagauthorsÅ¢kaffiliationmCisco SystemsdnamehP. Duffyddatej”8hfilenamegrfc3594eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymcdhcdfullx dhc - Dynamic Host ConfigurationdnamexDynamic Host Configurationdtypebwgbidjdoc-125544hkeywordsÑdDHCPx#dynamic host configuration protocolcCCCxCableLabs Client ConfigurationkobsoletedByÄepagesopublicationDate?_Z@granking
