monitoring job progress to be registered as OPTIONAL extensions to
IPP/1.0 [RFC2566] and IPP/1.1 [RFC2911].fadNameiNed Freeddarea£gacronymcappdfullwapp - Applications AreadnameqApplications AreagauthorsÉ¢kaffiliationqXerox CorporationdnamekT. Hastings¢kaffiliationtIBM Printing CompanydnamehH. Lewis¢kaffiliationxHitachi Koki Imaging SolutionsdnamejR. Bergmanddatej“òhfilenamegrfc3381eflags£mhiddenDefaultıiobsoletedıgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymcippdfullx ipp - Internet Printing ProtocoldnamexInternet Printing Protocoldtypebwgbidjdoc-125336hkeywordsÑgIPP-E-TxInternet Printing Protocolkapplicationjmedia typekobsoletedByÅd8011epagesopublicationDate=õx˚granking5crfcd3381irfcNumber5estateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnameqProposed Standarddslugbpsfstream¢dnamedIETFdslugdietfetitlex9Internet Printing Protocol (IPP): Job Progress AttributesdtypecrfciupdatedByÄ∂habstractyËThis document specifies 3 additional OPTIONAL operations for use with
the Internet Printing Protocol/1.0 (IPP) [RFC2565, RFC2566], and
IPP/1.1 [RFC2911, RFC2910].  The end user, operator, and
administrator Set-Job-Attributes and Set-Printer-Attributes
operations are used to modify IPP Job objects and Printer objects,
respectively.  The third administrator Get-Printer-Supported-Values
operation returns values that the IPP Printer will accept for setting
its 'xxx-supported' attributes.fadNameiNed Freeddarea£gacronymcappdfullwapp - Applications AreadnameqApplications AreagauthorsÑ¢kaffiliationqXerox CorporationdnamekT. Hastings¢kaffiliationjConsultantdnamejR. Herriot¢kaffiliationoIBM CorporationdnameiC. Kugler¢kaffiliationoIBM CorporationdnamehH. Lewisddatej”5hfilenamegrfc3380eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymcippdfullx ipp - Internet Printing ProtocoldnamexInternet Printing Protocoldtypebwgbidjdoc-125335hkeywordsÑgIPP-E-TxInternet Printing Protocolkapplicationjmedia typekobsoletedByÄepages;opublicationDate=ö#ægranking4crfcd3380irfcNumber4estateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnameqProposed Standarddslugbpsfstream¢dnamedIETFdslugdietfetitlex@Internet Printing Protocol (IPP): Job and Printer Set OperationsdtypecrfciupdatedByÄ∂habstractx“This document specifies the requirements for Delegated Path Validation
