pScott O. Bradnerdarea£gacronymcsubdfullqsub - Sub-IP AreadnamekSub-IP AreagauthorsÉ¢kaffiliationxLulea University of TechnologydnamejT. Worster¢kaffiliationoNortel NetworksdnamehA. Doria¢kaffiliationjConsultantdnamejJ. Buerkleddatej“yhfilenamegrfc3293eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymdgsmpdfullx)gsmp - General Switch Management Protocoldnamex"General Switch Management Protocoldtypebwgbidjdoc-125254hkeywordsÜdGSMPx"General Switch Management ProtocolcATMxAsynchronous Transfer ModecTCPxTransmission Control ProtocolkobsoletedByÄepages	opublicationDate=ÿ~granking›crfcd3293irfcNumber›estateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnameqProposed Standarddslugbpsfstream¢dnamedIETFdslugdietfetitlexñGeneral Switch Management Protocol (GSMP) Packet Encapsulations for Asynchronous Transfer Mode (ATM), Ethernet and Transmission Control Protocol (TCP)dtypecrfciupdatedByÄ∂habstracty≤This document describes the General Switch Management Protocol Version 3 (GSMPv3).  The GSMPv3 is an asymmetric protocol that allows one or more external switch controllers to establish and maintain the state of a label switch such as, an ATM, frame relay or MPLS switch.  The GSMPv3 allows control of both unicast and multicast switch connection state as well as control of switch system resources and QoS features. [STANDARDS-TRACK]fadNamepScott O. Bradnerdarea£gacronymcsubdfullqsub - Sub-IP AreadnamekSub-IP AreagauthorsÑ¢kaffiliationxLulea University of TechnologydnamehA. Doria¢kaffiliationoNortel NetworksdnamemF. Hellstrand¢kaffiliationoNortel NetworksdnamejK. Sundell¢kaffiliationjConsultantdnamejT. Worsterddatej“yhfilenamegrfc3292eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymdgsmpdfullx)gsmp - General Switch Management Protocoldnamex"General Switch Management Protocoldtypebwgbidjdoc-125253hkeywordsÜdGSMPxgeneral switch label protocolgunicastimulticastcqosrquality of servicekobsoletedByÄepagesâopublicationDate=◊€granking‹crfcd3292irfcNumber‹estateÅiPublishedfstatus¢d