 Level DefinitionsdtypecrfciupdatedByÅd9141µhabstractyThis memo defines an extension of the Management Information Base (MIB) for use with network management protocols in TCP/IP-based internets.  In particular, it defines objects for managing the insertion of interesting Circuit Interfaces into the ifTable.  This is important for circuits that must be used within other MIB modules which require an ifEntry.  It allows for integrated monitoring of circuits as well as routing to circuits using unaltered, pre-existing MIB modules. [STANDARDS-TRACK]darea£gacronymcintdfullsint - Internet AreadnamemInternet AreagauthorsÇ¢kaffiliationqParadyne NetworksdnamenR. Steinberger¢kaffiliationxRAD Data Communications Ltd.dnamekO. Nicklassddatej“)hfilenamegrfc3201eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedıegroup§gacronymhfrnetmibdfullx"frnetmib - Frame Relay Service MIBdnamewFrame Relay Service MIBdtypebwgbidjdoc-125164hkeywordsÇcmibxmanagement information basekobsoletedByÄepagesopublicationDate<1lÄgrankingÅcrfcd3201irfcNumberÅestateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnameqProposed Standarddslugbpsfstream¢dnamedIETFdslugdietfetitlexCDefinitions of Managed Objects for Circuit to Interface TranslationdtypecrfciupdatedByÅd9141µhabstract`darea£gacronymcgendfullrgen - General AreadnamelGeneral AreagauthorsÅ¢kaffiliationcISIdnameiS. Ginozaddatej…ûhfilenamegrfc3199eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymdnonedfullxnone - Individual SubmissionsdnamevIndividual Submissionsdtypegindividbididoc-43427hkeywordsÄkobsoletedByÄepagesopublicationDate>B†9grankingcrfcd3199irfcNumberestateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnamemInformationaldslugcinffstream¢dnamefLegacydslugflegacyetitlex2Request for Comments Summary RFC Numbers 3100-3199dtypecrfciupdatedByÄµhabstractycThis document is a glossary of policy-related terms.  It provides abbreviations, explanations, and recommendations for use of these terms.  The intent is to improve the comprehensibility and consistency of writing that deals wit