mentaldslugcexpfstream¢dnamedIETFdslugdietfetitlex%Domain Security Services using S/MIMEdtypecrfciupdatedByÄµhabstracty_This document describes the representation of identity information in POLICY_DATA object for supporting policy based admission control in the Resource ReSerVation Protocol (RSVP).  The goal of identity representation is to allow a process on a system to securely identify the owner and the application of the communicating process (e.g., user id) and convey this information in RSVP messages (PATH or RESV) in a secure manner.  We describe the encoding of identities as RSVP policy element.  We describe the processing rules to generate identity policy elements for multicast merged flows. [STANDARDS-TRACK]darea£gacronymcopsdfullx$ops - Operations and Management AreadnamexOperations and Management Areagauthorsá¢kaffiliationeInteldnamehS. Yadav¢kaffiliationeInteldnamekR. Yavatkar¢kaffiliationiMicrosoftdnamejR. Pabbati¢kaffiliationiMicrosoftdnamegP. Ford¢kaffiliationiMicrosoftdnamehT. Moore¢kaffiliationtPolicyConsulting.ComdnameiS. Herzog¢kaffiliationeInteldnamegR. Hessddatej”hfilenamegrfc3182eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymcrapdfullx"rap - Resource Allocation ProtocoldnamexResource Allocation Protocoldtypebwgbidjdoc-125147hkeywordsÇdRSVPxresource reservation protocolkobsoletedByÄepagesopublicationDate;∏pgrankingncrfcd3182irfcNumbernestateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnameqProposed Standarddslugbpsfstream¢dnamedIETFdslugdietfetitlex Identity Representation for RSVPdtypecrfciupdatedByÄµhabstractx‹This document describes a preemption priority policy element for use by signaled policy based admission protocols (such as the Resource ReSerVation Protocol (RSVP) and Common Open Policy Service (COPS). [STANDARDS-TRACK]darea£gacronymcopsdfullx$ops - Operations and Management AreadnamexOperations and Management AreagauthorsÅ¢kaffiliationtPolicyConsulting.ComdnameiS. Herzogddatej”hfilenamegrfc3181eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupda