s a basic set of managed objects for SNMP-based (Simple Network Management Protocol) management of the Baseline Privacy Interface (BPI), which provides data privacy for DOCSIS 1.0 (Data-Over- Cable Service Interface Specifications) compliant Cable Modems and Cable Modem Termination Systems.  This MIB is defined as an extension to the DOCSIS Radio Frequency Interface MIB, RFC 2670.  This memo provides information for the Internet community.darea£gacronymcopsdfullx$ops - Operations and Management AreadnamexOperations and Management AreagauthorsÅ¢kaffiliationmCisco SystemsdnameiR. Woundyddatej“¢hfilenamegrfc3083eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedıegroup§gacronymeipcdndfullx"ipcdn - IP over Cable Data NetworkdnamexIP over Cable Data Networkdtypebwgbidjdoc-125053hkeywordsÖcMIBcBPIodata-over-cableqservice interfacenspecificationskobsoletedByÄepages-opublicationDate:ûÄgrankingcrfcd3083irfcNumberestateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnamemInformationaldslugcinffstream¢dnamedIETFdslugdietfetitlex|Baseline Privacy Interface Management Information Base for DOCSIS Compliant Cable Modems and Cable Modem Termination SystemsdtypecrfciupdatedByÅd9141µhabstractyƒThe Service Location Protocol (SLP) provides mechanisms whereby service agent clients can advertise and user agent clients can query for services.  The design is very much demand-driven, so that user agents only obtain service information when they specifically ask for it.  There exists another class of user agent applications, however, that requires notification when a new service appears or disappears.  In the RFC 2608 design, these applications are forced to poll the network to catch changes.  In this document, we describe a protocol for allowing such clients to be notified when a change occurs, removing the need for polling.  This memo defines an Experimental Protocol for the Internet community.darea£gacronymcgendfullrgen - General AreadnamelGeneral AreagauthorsÇ¢kaffiliationpSun MicrosystemsdnamehJ. Kempf¢kaffili