ort MPLS forwarding along normally routed paths.  This memo provides information for the Internet community.darea£gacronymcrtgdfullrrtg - Routing AreadnamelRouting AreagauthorsÇ¢kaffiliationsCisco Systems, Inc.dnameiB. Thomas¢kaffiliationmZaffire, Inc.dnamegE. Grayddatej“&hfilenamegrfc3037eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymdmplsdfullx$mpls - Multiprotocol Label SwitchingdnamexMultiprotocol Label Switchingdtypebwgbidjdoc-125007hkeywordsÉelabelldistributionhprotocolkobsoletedByÄepagesopublicationDate:P9␀granking›crfcd3037irfcNumber›estateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnamemInformationaldslugcinffstream¢dnamedIETFdslugdietfetitleqLDP ApplicabilitydtypecrfciupdatedByÄµhabstractyA fundamental concept in MPLS is that two Label Switching Routers (LSRs) must agree on the meaning of the labels used to forward traffic between and through them.  This common understanding is achieved by using a set of procedures, called a label distribution protocol, by which one LSR informs another of label bindings it has made.  This document defines a set of such procedures called LDP (for Label Distribution Protocol) by which LSRs distribute labels to support MPLS forwarding along normally routed paths. [STANDARDS-TRACK]darea£gacronymcrtgdfullrrtg - Routing AreadnamelRouting AreagauthorsÖ¢kaffiliationtNortel Networks Inc.dnamelL. Andersson¢kaffiliationqEnnovate NetworksdnameiP. Doolan¢kaffiliationhIBM CorpdnamejN. Feldman¢kaffiliationmPhotonEx CorpdnamekA. Fredette¢kaffiliationsCisco Systems, Inc.dnameiB. Thomasddatej“%hfilenamegrfc3036eflags£mhiddenDefaultıiobsoletedıgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymdmplsdfullx$mpls - Multiprotocol Label SwitchingdnamexMultiprotocol Label Switchingdtypebwgbidjdoc-125006hkeywordsÉelabelldistributionhprotocolkobsoletedByÅd5036epagesÑopublicationDate:P9␀granking‹crfcd3036irfcNumber‹estateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnameqProposed Standarddslugbpsfstream¢dnamedIETFdslugdietfetitleqLDP SpecificationdtypecrfciupdatedByÄµhabstracty~This document extends and clarifies the relevant portions of RFC 3031 and RFC 3036 by specifying in more detail the procedures which to be used when distributing labels to or from ATM-LSRs, when those labels represent Forwarding Equivalence Classes (FECs, see RFC 3031) for which the routes are determined on a hop-by-hop basis by network layer routing algorithms. [STANDARDS-TRACK]darea£gacronymcrtgdfullrrtg - Routing AreadnamelRouting Areagauthorsá¢kaffiliationsCisco Systems, Inc.dnamehB. Davie¢kaffiliationsCisco Systems, Inc.dnamekJ. Lawrence¢kaffiliationsCisco Systems, Inc.dnamemK. McCloghrie¢kaffiliationsCisco Systems, Inc.dnamehE. Rosen¢kaffiliationsCisco Systems, Inc.dnamejG. Swallow¢kaffiliationpJuniper NetworksdnamejY. Rekhter¢kaffiliationwEnnovate Networks, Inc.dnameiP. Doolanddatej“%hfilenamegrfc3035eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymdmplsdfullx$mpls - Multiprotocol Label SwitchingdnamexMultiprotocol Label Switchingdtypebwgbidjdoc-125005hkeywordsÜdMPLSxmulti-protocol label switchingcATMxasynchronous transfer modecLDPxlabel distribution protocolkobsoletedByÄepagesopublicationDate:P9␀granking€crfcd3035irfcNumber€estateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnameqProposed Standarddslugbpsfstream¢dnamedIETFdslugdietfetitlex#MPLS using LDP and ATM VC SwitchingdtypecrfciupdatedByÄµhabstractxÉThis document defines the model and generic mechanisms for Multiprotocol Label Switching on Frame Relay networks. [STANDARDS-TRACK]darea£gacronymcrtgdfullrrtg - Routing AreadnamelRouting AreagauthorsÉ¢kaffiliationvTranswitch CorporationdnamehA. Conta¢kaffiliationhEnnovatednameiP. Doolan¢kaffiliationuVivace Networks, Inc.dnamehA. Malisddatej“%hfilenamegrfc3034eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymdmplsdfullx$mpls - Multiprotocol Label SwitchingdnamexMultiprotocol Label Switchingdtypebwgbidjdoc-125004hkeywordsÇdMPLSxmulti-protocol label switchingkobsoletedByÄepagesopublicationDate:P9␀granking⁄crfcd3034irfcNumber⁄estateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnameqProposed 