 describes a secret-key cryptosystem MISTY1, which is block cipher with a 128-bit key, a 64-bit block and a variable number of rounds.  It documents the algorithm description including key scheduling part and data randomizing part.  This memo provides information for the Internet community.darea£gacronymcgendfullrgen - General AreadnamelGeneral AreagauthorsÇ¢kaffiliationxMitsubishi Electric CorporationdnamegH. Ohta¢kaffiliationxMitsubishi Electric CorporationdnameiM. Matsuiddatej“Âhfilenamegrfc2994eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymdnonedfullxnone - Individual SubmissionsdnamevIndividual Submissionsdtypegindividbidjdoc-124967hkeywordsÑlcryptosystemhsecurityddatafstreamkobsoletedByÄepages
