dnonedfullxnone - Individual SubmissionsdnamevIndividual Submissionsdtypegindividbidjdoc-124944hkeywordsÑeIMAP4x internet message access protocolfclientfserverkobsoletedByÄepagesopublicationDate9÷‡grankingõcrfcd2971irfcNumberõestateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnameqProposed Standarddslugbpsfstream¢dnamefLegacydslugflegacyetitlerIMAP4 ID extensiondtypecrfciupdatedByÄµhabstracty©Drawing from experiences with the TISDAG (Technical Infrastructure for Swedish Directory Access Gateways) project, this document outlines an approach to providing the necessary infrastructure for integrating such widely-scattered servers into a single service, rather than attempting to mandate a single protocol and schema set for all participating servers to use.  This memo provides information for the Internet community.darea£gacronymcgendfullrgen - General AreadnamelGeneral AreagauthorsÇ¢kaffiliation`dnameiL. Daigle¢kaffiliation`dnamehT. Eklofddatej”hfilenamegrfc2970eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymdnonedfullxnone - Individual SubmissionsdnamevIndividual Submissionsdtypegindividbidjdoc-124943hkeywordsácidsjwhitepagesitechnicalninfrastructuregswedishfaccesshgatewayskobsoletedByÄepagesopublicationDate9÷‡grankingöcrfcd2970irfcNumberöestateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnamemInformationaldslugcinffstream¢dnamedIETFdslugdietfetitlexCArchitecture for Integrated Directory Services - Result from TISDAGdtypecrfciupdatedByÄµhabstractyAThis document catalogues some of the experiences gained in developing the necessary infrastructure for a national (i.e., multi-organizational) directory service and pilot deployment of the service in an environment with off-the-shelf directory service products.  This memo provides information for the Internet community.darea£gacronymcgendfullrgen - General AreadnamelGeneral AreagauthorsÇ¢kaffiliation`dnamehT. Eklof¢kaffiliation`dnameiL. Daigleddatej”hfilenamegrfc2969eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymdnonedfullxnone - Individual SubmissionsdnamevIndividual Submissionsdtypegindividbidjdoc-124942hkeywordsÖitechnicalninfrastructuregswedishfaccesshgatewayskobsoletedByÄepagesopublicationDate9÷‡grankingôcrfcd2969irfcNumberôestateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnamemInformationaldslugcinffstream¢dnamefLegacydslugflegacyetitlex8Wide Area Directory Deployment - Experiences from TISDAGdtypecrfciupdatedByÄµhabstractyLThis document defines the basic principle for establishing a mesh, that interoperating services should exchange index objects, according to the architecture of the mesh (e.g., hierarchical, or graph-like, preferably without loops!).  The Common Indexing Protocol (CIP) is designed to facilitate the creation not only of query referral indexes, but also of meshes of (loosely) affiliated referral indexes.  The purpose of such a mesh of servers is to implement some kind of distributed sharing of indexing and/or searching tasks across different servers.  So far, the TISDAG (Technical Infrastructure for Swedish Directory Access Gateways) project has focused on creating a single referral index; the obvious next step is to integrate that into a larger set of interoperating services.  This memo provides information for the Internet community.darea£gacronymcgendfullrgen - General AreadnamelGeneral AreagauthorsÇ¢kaffiliation`dnameiL. Daigle¢kaffiliation`dnamehT. Eklofddatej”hfilenamegrfc2968eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymdnonedfullxnone - Individual SubmissionsdnamevIndividual Submissionsdtypegindividbidjdoc-124941hkeywordsàitechnicalninfrastructuregswedishidirectoryfaccesshgatewaysdmesheindexkobsoletedByÄepages	opublicationDate9÷‡grankingòcrfcd2968irfcNumberòestateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnamemInformationaldslugcinffstream¢dnamefLegacydslugflegacyetitlex2Mesh of Multiple DAG servers - Results from TISDAGdtypecrfciupdatedByÄµhabstractyThe overarching goal of this project is to develop the necessary technical infrastructure to provide a single-access-point service for searching for whitepages information on Swedish Internet users.  This memo provides information for the Internet community.darea£gacronymcgendfullrgen - General AreadnamelGeneral AreagauthorsÇ¢kaffiliationxThinking Cat EnterprisesdnameiL. Daigle¢kaffiliationiCatalogixdnamejR. Hedbergddatej“Öhfilenamegrfc2967eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymdnonedfullxnone - Individual SubmissionsdnamevIndividual Submissionsdtypegindividbidjdoc-124940hkeywordsÉfsingleepointgservicekobsoletedByÄepagesiopublicationDate9÷‡grankingócrfcd2967irfcNumberóestateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnamemInformationaldslugcinffstream¢dnamefLegacydslugflegacyetitlexGTISDAG - Technical Infrastructure for Swedish Directory Access GatewaysdtypecrfciupdatedByÄ∂habstractx◊This document describes extensions to the Intermediate System to Intermediate System (IS-IS) protocol to support optimal routing within a two-level domain.  This memo provides information for the Internet community.fadNamekRoss Callondarea£gacronymcrtgdfullrrtg - Routing AreadnamelRouting AreagauthorsÉ¢kaffiliationpProcket NetworksdnameeT. Li¢kaffiliationgRedbackdnamemT. Przygienda¢kaffiliationpProcket NetworksdnamegH. Smitddatej“Éhfilenamegrfc2966eflags£mhiddenDefaultıiobsoletedıgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymdisisdfullxisis - IS-IS for IP InternetsdnamevIS-IS for IP Internetsdtypebwgbidjdoc-124939hkeywordsálintermediatefsystemgrouterseloopsbIPhinternethprotocolkobsoletedByÅd5302epagesopublicationDate9÷‡grankingñcrfcd2966irfcNumberñestateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnamemInformationaldslugcinffstream¢dnamedIETFdslugdietfetitlex4Domain-wide Prefix Distribution with Two-Level IS-ISdtypecrfciupdatedByÄµhabstractxåThis document specifies a way to create a stateful session with Hypertext Transfer Protocol (HTTP) requests and responses. [STANDARDS-TRACK]darea£gacronymcappdfullwapp - Applications AreadnameqApplications AreagauthorsÇ¢kaffiliationx&Bell Laboratories, Lucent TechnologiesdnamejD. Kristol¢kaffiliationrEpinion