teÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnamemInformationaldslugcinffstream¢dnamedIETFdslugdietfetitlex3Call Processing Language Framework and RequirementsdtypecrfciupdatedByÄµhabstractyTThis document extends methods found in the Point-to-Point Protocol (PPP) and RFCs 1662 and 2615 to include a new encapsulation for PPP called Simple Data Link (SDL).  SDL provides a standard method for transporting multi-protocol datagrams over point-to-point links, and RFCs 1662 and 2615 provide a means to carry PPP over Synchronous Optical Network (SONET) and Synchronous Digital Hierarchy (SDH) circuits.  SDL provides a very low overhead alternative to HDLC-like encapsulation, and can also be used on SONET/SDH links.  This memo defines an Experimental Protocol for the Internet community.darea£gacronymcintdfullsint - Internet AreadnamemInternet AreagauthorsÑ¢kaffiliationvSun Microsystems, Inc.dnamejJ. Carlson¢kaffiliationx*Lucent Technologies Microelectronics GroupdnamejP. Langner¢kaffiliationsLucent TechnologiesdnameuE. Hernandez-Valencia¢kaffiliationsLucent TechnologiesdnamemJ. Manchesterddatej“øhfilenamegrfc2823eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymfpppextdfullx+pppext - Point-to-Point Protocol Extensionsdnamex"Point-to-Point Protocol Extensionsdtypebwgbidjdoc-124798hkeywordságPPP-SDLwpoint-to-point protocolpSimple Data LinkeSONETxsynchronous optical networkcSDHxsynchronous digital hierarchykobsoletedByÄepagesopublicationDate9+pgrankingcrfcd2823irfcNumberestateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnamelExperimentaldslugcexpfstream¢dnamedIETFdslugdietfetitlexEPPP over Simple Data Link (SDL) using SONET/SDH with ATM-like framingdtypecrfciupdatedByÄµhabstractxûThis document specifies a syntax for text messages that are sent between computer users, within the framework of "electronic mail" messages. [STANDARDS-TRACK]darea£gacronymcappdfullwapp - Applications AreadnameqApplications AreagauthorsÅ¢kaffiliationuQUALCOMM IncorporateddnamejP. Resnickddatej—~hfilenamegrfc2822eflags£mhiddenD