 the resource identified by a Uniform Resource Identifier (URI) is only one of the operations that can be performed on a URI.  One might also ask for and get a list of other identifiers that are aliases for the original URI or a bibliographic description of the resource the URI denotes, for example.  This applies to both Uniform Resource Names (URNs) and Uniform Resource Locators (URLs).  Uniform Resource Characteristics (URCs) are discussed in this document but only as descriptions of resources rather than identifiers.  This memo defines an Experimental Protocol for the Internet community.darea£gacronymcappdfullwapp - Applications AreadnameqApplications AreagauthorsÇ¢kaffiliationqNetwork SolutionsdnamekM. Mealling¢kaffiliationxLos Alamos National LaboratorydnameiR. Danielddatej“hfilenamegrfc2483eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymcurndfullxurn - Uniform Resource NamesdnamevUniform Resource Namesdtypebwgbidjdoc-124473hkeywordsÜcURIxuniform resource identifiercURNvuniform resource nameshlocatorsocharacteristicskobsoletedByÄepagesopublicationDate6åÄÄgranking	≥crfcd2483irfcNumber	≥estateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnamelExperimentaldslugcexpfstream¢dnamedIETFdslugdietfetitlex4URI Resolution Services Necessary for URN ResolutiondtypecrfciupdatedByÄµhabstractxÇThis document proposed a mechanism for language tagging in plain text.  This memo provides information for the Internet community.darea£gacronymcgendfullrgen - General AreadnamelGeneral AreagauthorsÇ¢kaffiliationfSybasednamekK. Whistler¢kaffiliationhSpyglassdnamehG. Adamsddatej“hfilenamegrfc2482eflags£mhiddenDefaultıiobsoletedıgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymdnonedfullxnone - Individual SubmissionsdnamevIndividual Submissionsdtypegindividbidjdoc-124472hkeywordsÉjcharactersgstringseASCIIkobsoletedByÅd6082epagesopublicationDate6åÄÄgranking	≤crfcd2482irfcNumber	≤estateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnamehHistoricdslugdhistfstream¢dnamefLegacydslugflegacyetitlex&Language Tagging in Unicode Plain Textdtypecrfc