ersion 2.0dtypecrfciupdatedByÄµhabstractyñHTTP allows web site authors to put multiple versions of the same information under a single URL.  Transparent content negotiation is a mechanism for automatically selecting the best version when the URL is accessed.  A remote variant selection algorithm can be used to speed up the transparent negotiation process.  This document defines the remote variant selection algorithm with the version number 1.0.darea£gacronymcappdfullwapp - Applications AreadnameqApplications AreagauthorsÇ¢kaffiliationx!Technische Universiteit EindhovendnamejK. Holtman¢kaffiliationwHewlett-Packard CompanydnamegA. Mutzddatej“îhfilenamegrfc2296eflags£mhiddenDefaultıiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymdhttpdfullx"http - HyperText Transfer ProtocoldnamexHyperText Transfer Protocoldtypebwgbidjdoc-124299hkeywordsâiHTTP-RVSAeHyperdTexthTransferhprotocolcURLgUniformhResourcehLocatorskobsoletedByÄepagesopublicationDate4˘Ägranking¯crfcd2296irfcNumber¯estateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnamehHistoricdslugdhistfstream¢dnamedIETFdslugdietfetitlex3HTTP Remote Variant Selection Algorithm -- RVSA/1.0dtypecrfciupdatedByÄµhabstractyHTTP allows web site authors to put multiple versions of the same information under a single URL.  Transparent content negotiation is an extensible negotiation mechanism, layered on top of HTTP, for automatically selecting the best version when the URL is accessed.  This enables the smooth deployment of new web data formats and markup tags.  This memo defines an Experimental Protocol for the Internet community.  It does not specify an Internet standard of any kind.  Discussion and suggestions for improvement are requested.darea£gacronymcappdfullwapp - Applications AreadnameqApplications AreagauthorsÇ¢kaffiliationx!Technische Universiteit EindhovendnamejK. Holtman¢kaffiliationwHewlett-Packard CompanydnamegA. Mutzddatej“îhfilenamegrfc2295eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymdhttpdfullx"http - HyperText Transfer Protoco