 from one machine to another transparently, and a mechanism by which people or agents may programmatically discover that an organization runs, say, a World-Wide Web server.  Although this approach has been almost universally adopted, there is no standards document or similar specification for these commonly used names.  This document seeks to rectify this situation by gathering together the extant 'folklore' on naming conventions, and proposes a mechanism for accommodating new protocols.  This document specifies an Internet Best Current Practices for the Internet Community, and requests discussion and suggestions for improvements.darea£gacronymcappdfullwapp - Applications AreadnameqApplications AreagauthorsÇ¢kaffiliationx%Loughborough University of TechnologydnamekM. Hamilton¢kaffiliationx%Lawrence Berkeley National LaboratorydnameiR. Wrightddatej”hfilenamegrfc2219eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymcidsdfullx#ids - Integrated Directory ServicesdnamexIntegrated Directory Servicesdtypebwgbidjdoc-124229hkeywordsÑfdomaindnamefsystemhsymbolickobsoletedByÄepagesopublicationDate41Ùgranking´crfcd2219irfcNumber´estateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnameuBest Current Practicedslugcbcpfstream¢dnamedIETFdslugdietfisubseries£gacronymcbcpfnumberetotaletitlex'Use of DNS Aliases for Network ServicesdtypecrfciupdatedByÄµhabstractx«This document specifies the minimum set of core attributes of a White Pages entry for an individual and describes how new objects with those attributes can be defined and published. [STANDARDS-TRACK]darea£gacronymcappdfullwapp - Applications AreadnameqApplications AreagauthorsÇ¢kaffiliationuMicrosoft CorporationdnamekT. Genovese¢kaffiliationxSandia National LaboratoriesdnamekB. Jenningsddatej”hfilenamegrfc2218eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymcidsdfullx#ids - Integrated Directory ServicesdnamexIntegrated Directory Servicesdtypebwgbidjdoc-124228hkeywordsÉdIWPSkinformationduserkobsoletedByÄepagesopublicatio