crfciupdatedByád5452d2535d8767d4033d4034d4035d4343µhabstractyÒThe behavior described in this document reflects the practice of some existing servers or behavior that the consensus of the IMAP mailing list has deemed to be reasonable.  The behavior described within this document is believed to be [RFC-2060] compliant.  However, this document is not meant to define IMAP4 compliance, nor is it an exhaustive list of valid IMAP4 behavior.  This memo provides information for the Internet community.  This memo does not specify an Internet standard of any kind.darea£gacronymcgendfullrgen - General AreadnamelGeneral AreagauthorsÅ¢kaffiliationiMicrosoftdnameiM. Gahrnsddatej“>hfilenamegrfc2180eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymdnonedfullxnone - Individual SubmissionsdnamevIndividual Submissionsdtypegindividbidjdoc-124193hkeywordsÜhInternetgMessagefAccesshProtocolfClientfServerkobsoletedByÄepagesopublicationDate3∏™grankingÑcrfcd2180irfcNumberÑestateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnamemInformationaldslugcinffstream¢dnamefLegacydslugflegacyetitlex%IMAP4 Multi-Accessed Mailbox PracticedtypecrfciupdatedByÄµhabstractyHThis document is designed to assist vendors and other participants in trade shows, such as Networld+Interop, in designing effective protection against network and system attacks by unauthorized individuals.  This memo provides information for the Internet community.  This memo does not specify an Internet standard of any kind.darea£gacronymcgendfullrgen - General AreadnamelGeneral AreagauthorsÅ¢kaffiliationxSouthern Methodist UniversitydnamehA. Gwinnddatej“>hfilenamegrfc2179eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymdnonedfullxnone - Individual SubmissionsdnamevIndividual Submissionsdtypegindividbidjdoc-124192hkeywordsÉgnetworkfsystemgattackskobsoletedByÄepages
opublicationDate3∏™grankingÉcrfcd2179irfcNumberÉestateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnamemInformationaldslugcinffstream¢dnamefLegacydslugflegacyetitlex Network Security For Trade ShowsdtypecrfciupdatedByÄµhabstracty÷This memo documents version 2 of the OSPF protocol. OSPF is a link-state routing protocol. It is designed to be run internal to a single Autonomous System. Each OSPF router maintains an identical database describing the Autonomous System's topology. From this database, a routing table is calculated by constructing a shortest-path tree.

OSPF recalculates routes quickly in the face of topological changes, utilizing a minimum of routing protocol traffic. OSPF provides support for equal-cost multipath. An area routing capability is provided, enabling an additional level of routing protection and a reduction in routing protocol traffic. In addition, all OSPF routing protocol exchanges are authenticated. [STANDARDS-TRACK]darea£gacronymcrtgdfullrrtg - Routing AreadnamelRouting AreagauthorsÅ¢kaffiliationxCascade Communications Corp.dnamefJ. Moyddatej“=hfilenamegrfc2178eflags£mhiddenDefaultıiobsoletedıgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymdospfdfullx#ospf - Open Shortest Path First IGPdnamexOpen Shortest Path First IGPdtypebwgbidjdoc-124191hkeywordsàdOpenhShortestdPatheFirstgroutingjAutonomousfsystembASkobsoletedByÅd2328epages”opublicationDate3∏™grankingÇcrfcd2178irfcNumberÇestateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnamenDraft Standarddslugbdsfstream¢dnamedIETFdslugdietfetitlenOSPF Version 2dtypecrfciupdatedByÄµhabstractxßThis document specifies the syntax of an IDLE command, which will allow a client to tell the server that it's ready to accept such real-time updates. [STANDARDS-TRACK]darea£gacronymcgendfullrgen - General AreadnamelGeneral AreagauthorsÅ¢kaffiliation`dnamehB. Leibaddatej“_hfilenamegrfc2177eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymdnonedfullxnone - Individual SubmissionsdnamevIndividual Submissionsdtypegindividbidjdoc-124190hkeywordsÅjIMAP4-IDLEkobsoletedByÄepagesopublicationDate3ëgrankingÅcrfcd2177irfcNumberÅestateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnameqProposed Standarddslugbpsfstream¢dnamefLegacydslugflegacyetitlerIMAP4 IDLE commanddtypecrfciupdatedByÄµhabstractyThis memo documents a mechanism for supporting Version 4 of the Internet Protocol (IPv4) on Version 1 of the Multiple Access Protocol over SONET/SDH.  This memo provides information for the Internet community.  This memo does not specify an Internet standard of any kind.darea£gacronymcgendfullrgen - General AreadnamelGeneral AreagauthorsÇ¢kaffiliation`dnamekK. Murakami¢kaffiliation`dnamekM. Maruyamaddatej“^hfilenamegrfc2176eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedıegroup§gacronymdnonedfullxnone - Individual SubmissionsdnamevIndividual Submissionsdtypegindividbidjdoc-124189hkeywordsÅjIPV4-MAPOSkobsoletedByÄepagesopublicationDate3ëgrankingÄcrfcd2176irfcNumberÄestateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnamemInformationaldslugcinffstream¢dnamefLegacydslugflegacyetitlexIPv4 over MAPOS Version 1dtypecrfciupdatedByÅd5494µhabstracty&This memo documents MAPOS 16, a multiple access protocol for transmission of network-protocol datagrams, encapsulated in HDLC frames with 16 bit addressing, over SONET/SDH.  This memo provides information for the Internet community.  This memo does not specify an Internet standard of any kind.darea£gacronymcgendfullrgen - General AreadnamelGeneral AreagauthorsÇ¢kaffiliation`dnamekK. Murakami¢kaffiliation`dnamekM. Maruyamaddatej 5hfilenamegrfc2175eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymdnonedfullxnone - Individual SubmissionsdnamevIndividual Submissionsdtypegindividbidjdoc-124188hkeywordsÄkobsoletedByÄepagesopublicationDate3ëgrankingcrfcd2175irfcNumberestateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnamemInformationaldslugcinffstream¢dnamefLegacydslugflegacyetitlexIMAPOS 16 - Multiple Access Protocol over SONET/SDH with 16 Bit AddressingdtypecrfciupdatedByÄµhabstracty1This memo documents a MAPOS (Multiple Access Protocol over SONET/SDH) version 1 extension, Switch Switch Protocol which provides dynamic routing for unicast, broadcast, and multicast.  This memo provides information for the Internet community.  This memo does not specify an Internet standard of any kind.darea£gacronymcgendfullrgen - General AreadnamelGeneral AreagauthorsÇ¢kaffiliation`dnamekK. Murakami¢kaffiliation`dnamekM. Maruyamaddatej 5hfilenamegrfc2174eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymdnonedfullxnone - Individual SubmissionsdnamevIndividual Submissionsdtypegindividbidjdoc-124187h