This document relates primarily to the ITU-T 1988 and 1992 X.400 Series Recommendations / ISO IEC 10021 International Standard.  This ISO/ITU-T standard is referred to in this document as "X.400", which is a convenient shorthand. [STANDARDS-TRACK]darea£gacronymcappdfullwapp - Applications AreadnameqApplications AreagauthorsÅ¢kaffiliationiIsode LtddnamehS. Killeddatej“hfilenamegrfc2156eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymemixerdfullxmixer - MIME - X.400 GatewaydnametMIME - X.400 Gatewaydtypebwgbidjdoc-124169hkeywordsàeMIXERlmultipurposehinternetdmailjextensionsgmessagehtransferhprotocolkobsoletedByÄepagesêopublicationDate4´M␀grankinglcrfcd2156irfcNumberlestateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnameqProposed Standarddslugbpsfstream¢dnamedIETFdslugdietfetitlexRMIXER (Mime Internet X.400 Enhanced Relay): Mapping between X.400 and RFC 822/MIMEdtypecrfciupdatedByÄµhabstractyeThis memo defines a portion of the Management Information Base (MIB) for use with network management protocols in the Internet community.  In particular, it defines objects for monitoring and controlling network devices with APPN (Advanced Peer-to-Peer Networking) capabilities.  This memo identifies managed objects for the APPN protocol. [STANDARDS-TRACK]darea£gacronymcrtgdfullrrtg - Routing AreadnamelRouting AreagauthorsÇ¢kaffiliation`dnamekB. Clouston¢kaffiliation`dnamehB. Mooreddatej“^hfilenamegrfc2155eflags£mhiddenDefaultıiobsoletedıgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymfsnanaudfullxsnanau - SNA NAU Services MIBdnametSNA NAU Services MIBdtypebwgbidjdoc-124168hkeywordsÅhAPPN-MIBkobsoletedByÅd2455epages|opublicationDate3ëgrankingkcrfcd2155irfcNumberkestateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnameqProposed Standarddslugbpsfstream¢dnamedIETFdslugdietfetitlex3Definitions of Managed Objects for APPN using SMIv2dtypecrfciupdatedByÄµhabstractyzThis memo describes the extensions to OSPF required to add digital signature authentication to Link State data, and to provide a certification mechanism for router data.  Added LSA processing and key management is detailed.  A method for migration from, or co-existence with, standard OSPF V2 is described.  This memo defines an Experimental Protocol for the Internet community.darea£gacronymcgendfullrgen - General AreadnamelGeneral AreagauthorsÉ¢kaffiliation`dnameiS. Murphy¢kaffiliation`dnameiM. Badger¢kaffiliation`dnamemB. Wellingtonddatej“^hfilenamegrfc2154eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymdnonedfullxnone - Individual SubmissionsdnamevIndividual Submissionsdtypegindividbidjdoc-124167hkeywordsÅhOSPF-DIGkobsoletedByÄepagesopublicationDate3ëgrankingjcrfcd2154irfcNumberjestateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnamelExperimentaldslugcexpfstream¢dnamefLegacydslugflegacyetitlexOSPF with Digital SignaturesdtypecrfciupdatedByÄµhabstractyÈThe Point-to-Point Protocol (PPP) provides a standard method for transporting multi-protocol datagrams over point-to-point links.  PPP defines an extensible Link Control Protocol (LCP) for establishing, configuring, and testing the data-link connection; and a family of Network Control Protocols (NCPs) for establishing and configuring different network-layer protocols.  This document provides information for the Internet community.  It does not specify an Internet standard of any kind.darea£gacronymcintdfullsint - Internet AreadnamemInternet AreagauthorsÅ¢kaffiliationjDayDreamerdnamejW. Simpsonddatej“∏hfilenamegrfc2153eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedıegroup§gacronymfpppextdfullx+pppext - Point-to-Point Protocol Extensionsdnamex"Point-to-Point Protocol Extensionsdtypebwgbidjdoc-124166hkeywordsÉgPPP-EXTnPoint-to-PointhProtocolkobsoletedByÄepagesopublicationDate3h?pgrankingicrfcd2153irfcNumberiestateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnamemInformationaldslugcinffstream¢dnamedIETFdslugdietfetitleuPPP Vendor ExtensionsdtypecrfciupdatedByÇd7042d5342µhabstractyŸThis document describes a transformation format of Unicode that contains only 7-bit ASCII octets and is intended to be readable by humans in the limiting case that the document consists of characters from the US-ASCII repertoire.  It also specifies how this transformation format is used in the context of MIME and RFC 1641, "Using Unicode with MIME".  This memo provides information for the Internet community.  This memo does not specify an Internet standard of any kind.darea£gacronymcgendfullrgen - General AreadnamelGeneral AreagauthorsÇ¢kaffiliationtApple Computer, Inc.dnamelD. Goldsmith¢kaffiliationnTaligent, Inc.dnamehM. Davisddatej“∏hfilenamegrfc2152eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymdnonedfullxnone - Individual SubmissionsdnamevIndividual Submissionsdtypegindividbidjdoc-124165hkeywordsÅeUTF-7kobsoletedByÄepagesopublicationDate3h?pgrankinghcrfcd2152irfcNumberhestateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnamemInformationaldslugcinffstream¢dnamefLegacydslugflegacyetitlex2UTF-7 A Mail-Safe Transformation Format of UnicodedtypecrfciupdatedByÄ∂habstracty¶This memo is an introductory guide to many of the most commonly- available TCP/IP and Internet tools and utilities.  It also describes discussion lists accessible from the Internet, ways to obtain Internet and TCP/IP documents, and some resources that help users weave their way through the Internet.  This memo provides information for the Internet community.  This memo does not specify an Internet standard of any kind.darea£gacronymcgendfullrgen - General AreadnamelGeneral AreagauthorsÇ¢kaffiliation`dnamejG. Kessler¢kaffiliation`dnamejS. Shepardddatej“]hfilenamegrfc2151eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymdnonedfullxnone - Individual SubmissionsdnamevIndividual Submissionsdtypegindividbidjdoc-124164hkeywordsÉhresourceeguideduserkobsoletedByÄepages4opublicationDate3ëgrankinggcrfcd2151irfcNumbergestateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnamemInformationaldslugcinffstream¢dnamefLegacydslugflegacyisubseries£gacronymcfyifnumberetotaletitlex3A Primer On Internet and TCP/IP Tools and UtilitiesdtypecrfciupdatedByÄ∂habstractyqThe purpose of this document is to provide members of the Arts and Humanities communities with an introduction to the Internet as a valuable tool, resource, and medium for the creation, presentation, and preservation of Arts and Humanities-based content.  This memo provides information for the Internet community.  It does not specify an Internet standard of any kind.darea£gacronymcusvdfullxusv - User Services AreadnamerUser Services AreagauthorsÇ¢kaffiliationhRainfarmdnamefJ. Max¢kaffiliationhRainfarmdnamejW. Stickleddatej”hfilenamegrfc2150eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymehartsdfullxharts - Humanities and ArtsdnamesHumanities and Artsdtypebwgbidjdoc-124163hkeywordsÑminformationalninfrastructureeguidelintroductionkobsoletedByÄepages>opublicationDate41Ùgrankingfcrfcd2150irfcNumberfestateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnamemInformationaldslugcinffstream¢dnamedIETFdslugdietfisubseries£gacronymcfyifnumberetotaletitlex9Humanities and Arts: Sharing Center Stage on the InternetdtypecrfciupdatedByÄµhabstractyœThis memo provides details on the design and implementation of an MCS, building on the core mechanisms defined in RFC 2022.  It also provides a mechanism for using multiple MCSs per group for providing fault tolerance.  This approach can be used with RFC 2022 based MARS server and clients, without needing any change in their functionality.  This memo provides information for the Internet community.  This memo does not specify an Internet standard of any kind.darea£gacronymcintdfullsint - Internet AreadnamemInternet AreagauthorsÇ¢kaffiliationxGeorgia Institute of TechnologydnamejR. Talpade¢kaffiliationxGeorgia Institute of TechnologydnamehM. Ammarddatej ≥hfilenamegrfc2149eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymciondfullxion - Internetworking Over NBMAdnamexInternetworking Over NBMAdtypebwgbidjdoc-124162hkeywordsÄkobsoletedByÄepagesopublicationDate3h?pgrankingecrfcd2149irfcNumbereestateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnamem