osed Standarddslugbpsfstream¢dnamedIETFdslugdietfetitlex*The PPP Compression Control Protocol (CCP)dtypecrfciupdatedByÅd2153µhabstractxﬂThis document provides the specification for the SOCKS V5 GSS-API authentication protocol, and defines a GSS-API-based encapsulation for provision of integrity, authentication and optional confidentiality. [STANDARDS-TRACK]darea£gacronymcsecdfullssec - Security AreadnamemSecurity AreagauthorsÅ¢kaffiliationcICLdnamejP. McMahonddatej“\hfilenamegrfc1961eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymcaftdfullx&aft - Authenticated Firewall Traversaldnamex Authenticated Firewall Traversaldtypebwgbidjdoc-123982hkeywordsájGSSAPI-SOCgGenerichSecuritygServicekApplicationgProgramiInterfacekobsoletedByÄepages	opublicationDate1ØÍpgranking©crfcd1961irfcNumber©estateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnameqProposed Standarddslugbpsfstream¢dnamedIETFdslugdietfetitlex1GSS-API Authentication Method for SOCKS Version 5dtypecrfciupdatedByÄµhabstractyoThe Lightweight Directory Access Protocol (LDAP) [1] defines a network representation of a search filter transmitted to an LDAP server.  Some applications may find it useful to have a common way of representing these search filters in a human-readable form.  This document defines a human-readable string format for representing LDAP search filters. [STANDARDS-TRACK]darea£gacronymcappdfullwapp - Applications AreadnameqApplications AreagauthorsÅ¢kaffiliationvUniversity of MichigandnamehT. Howesddatej“\hfilenamegrfc1960eflags£mhiddenDefaultıiobsoletedıgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymdasiddfullx4asid - Access, Searching and Indexing of Directoriesdnamex-Access, Searching and Indexing of Directoriesdtypebwgbidjdoc-123981hkeywordsÖhLDAP-STRkLightweightiDirectoryfAccesshProtocolkobsoletedByÅd2254epagesopublicationDate1ØÍpgranking®crfcd1960irfcNumber®estateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnameqProposed Standarddslugbpsfstream¢dnamedIETFdslugdietfetitlex.A String Representation of LDAP Search FiltersdtypecrfciupdatedByÄµhabstr