roup§gacronymfipngwgdfullmipngwg - IPNGdnamedIPNGdtypebwgbidjdoc-123927hkeywordsÑhInternethProtocoliprototypehsoftwarekobsoletedByÅd2471epagesopublicationDate0ÁîÄgrankingicrfcd1897irfcNumberiestateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnamelExperimentaldslugcexpfstream¢dnamedIETFdslugdietfetitlexIPv6 Testing Address AllocationdtypecrfciupdatedByÄµhabstractxŒThis document defines one particular type of MIME data, the text/enriched MIME type.  This memo provides information for the Internet community.  This memo does not specify an Internet standard of any kind.darea£gacronymcgendfullrgen - General AreadnamelGeneral AreagauthorsÇ¢kaffiliationhQUALCOMMdnamejP. Resnick¢kaffiliationhInterCondnameiA. Walkerddatej—Èhfilenamegrfc1896eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymdnonedfullxnone - Individual SubmissionsdnamevIndividual Submissionsdtypegindividbidjdoc-123926hkeywordsÖdMIMElMultipurposehInternetdMailjExtensionskobsoletedByÄepagesopublicationDate1s␀grankinghcrfcd1896irfcNumberhestateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnamemInformationaldslugcinffstream¢dnamefLegacydslugflegacyetitlex#The text/enriched MIME Content-typedtypecrfciupdatedByÄµhabstractydThis memorandum provides guidelines for using the United States Department of Defense Military Standard MIL-STD-1840, "Automated Interchange of Technical Information," with the Internet electronic mail standards, RFC 822 and RFC 1521.  This memo provides information for the Internet community.  This memo does not specify an Internet standard of any kind.darea£gacronymcgendfullrgen - General AreadnamelGeneral AreagauthorsÅ¢kaffiliationx"Accurate Information Systems, Inc.dnamekE. Levinsonddatej—Èhfilenamegrfc1895eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymdnonedfullxnone - Individual SubmissionsdnamevIndividual Submissionsdtypegindividbididoc-43322hkeywordsÜlMIL-STD-1840dMIMElMultipurposehInternetdMailjExtensionskobsoletedByÄepagesopublicationDate1s␀grankinggcrfcd1895irfcNumbergestateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnamemInformationaldslugcinffstream¢dnamefLegacydslugflegacyetitlex&The Application/CALS-1840 Content-typedtypecrfciupdatedByÄµhabstractxÿThis memo defines a MIME content-type that may be used by a message transfer agent (MTA) or electronic mail gateway to report the result of an attempt to deliver a message to one or more recipients. [STANDARDS-TRACK]darea£gacronymcappdfullwapp - Applications AreadnameqApplications AreagauthorsÇ¢kaffiliationwUniversity of TennesseednamehK. Moore¢kaffiliationvOctel Network ServicesdnamelG. Vaudreuilddatej“hfilenamegrfc1894eflags£mhiddenDefaultıiobsoletedıgupdatedıegroup§gacronymfnotarydfullx8notary - Notifications and Acknowledgements Requirementsdnamex/Notifications and Acknowledgements Requirementsdtypebwgbidjdoc-123925hkeywordsácDSNlMultipurposehInternetdMailjExtensionsgContentdTypekobsoletedByÅd3464epages'opublicationDate0ÁîÄgrankingfcrfcd1894irfcNumberfestateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnameqProposed Standarddslugbpsfstream¢dnamedIETFdslugdietfetitlex>An Extensible Message Format for Delivery Status NotificationsdtypecrfciupdatedByÅd2852µhabstractyáThere currently is not a standard mechanism for the reporting of mail system errors except for the limited set offered by SMTP and the system specific text descriptions sent in mail messages.  There is a pressing need for a rich machine readable status code for use in delivery status notifications [DSN].  This document proposes a new set of status codes for this purpose. [STANDARDS-TRACK]darea£gacronymcappdfullwapp - Applications AreadnameqApplications AreagauthorsÅ¢kaffiliationuOctel Network ServicednamelG. Vaudreuilddatej“hfilenamegrfc1893eflags£mhiddenDefaultıiobsoletedıgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymfnotarydfullx8notary - Notifications and Acknowledgements Requirementsdnamex/Notifications and Acknowledgements Requirementsdtypebwgbidjdoc-123924hkeywordsÜhEMS-CODEfsimpledmailhtransferhprotocoldSMTPkobsoletedByÅd3463epagesopublicationDate0ÁîÄgrankingecrfcd1893irfcNumbereestateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnameqProposed Standarddslugbpsfstream¢dnamedIETFdslugdietfetitlex!Enhanced Mail System Status CodesdtypecrfciupdatedByÄµhabstractyfThe Multipart/Report MIME content-type is a general "family" or "container" type for electronic mail reports of any kind.  Although this memo defines only the use of the Multipart/Report content-type with respect to delivery status reports, mail processing programs will benefit if a single content-type is used to for all kinds of reports. [STANDARDS-TRACK]darea£gacronymcappdfullwapp - Applications AreadnameqApplications AreagauthorsÅ¢kaffiliationuOctel Network ServicednamelG. Vaudreuilddatej“hfilenamegrfc1892eflags£mhiddenDefaultıiobsoletedıgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymfnotarydfullx8notary - Notifications and Acknowledgements Requirementsdnamex/Notifications and Acknowledgements Requirementsdtypebwgbidjdoc-123923hkeywordsÖhMIME-RPTlMultipurposehInternetdMailjExtensionskobsoletedByÅd3462epagesopublicationDate0ÁîÄgrankingdcrfcd1892irfcNumberdestateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnameqProposed Standarddslugbpsfstream¢dnamedIETFdslugdietfetitlexZThe Multipart/Report Content Type for the Reporting of Mail System Administrative MessagesdtypecrfciupdatedByÄµhabstracty‡This memo defines an extension to the SMTP service, which allows an SMTP client to specify (a) that delivery status notifications (DSNs) should be generated under certain conditions, (b) whether such notifications should return the contents of the message, and (c) additional information, to be returned with a DSN, that allows the sender to identify both the recipient(s) for which the DSN was issued, and the transaction in which the original message was sent. [STANDARDS-TRACK]darea£gacronymcappdfullwapp - Applications AreadnameqApplications AreagauthorsÅ¢kaffiliationwUniversity of TennesseednamehK. Mooreddatej“
