nts, rapidly acquiring the nickname "Son of 1036". Indeed, under that name, it could fairly be described as the best-known Internet Draft (n)ever published, and it formed the starting point for the recently adopted Proposed Standards for Netnews.

It is being published now in order to provide the historical background out of which those standards have grown. Present-day implementors should be aware that it is NOT NOW APPROPRIATE for use in current implementations. This document defines a Historic Document for the Internet community.fadNameqLisa M. DusseaultgauthorsÅ¢kaffiliationjSP SystemsdnamejH. Spencerddatej‘Whfilenamegrfc1849eflags£mhiddenDefaultıiobsoletedıgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymcappdfullwapp - Applications AreadnameqApplications Areadtypedareabidjdoc-123885hkeywordsÖgnetnewsfusenethrfc 1036fuseforhhistorickobsoletedByÇd5536d5537epagesjopublicationDateK≠Fügranking9crfcd1849irfcNumber9estateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnamehHistoricdslugdhistfstream¢dnamecISEdslugciseetitlex3"Son of 1036": News Article Format and TransmissiondtypecrfciupdatedByÄµhabstractx·This document defines MIME Object Security Services (MOSS), a protocol that uses the multipart/signed and multipart/encrypted framework [7] to apply digital signature and encryption services to MIME objects. [STANDARDS-TRACK]darea£gacronymcsecdfullssec - Security AreadnamemSecurity AreagauthorsÑ¢kaffiliationiCybercashdnamejS. Crocker¢kaffiliationhInnosoftdnamehN. Freed¢kaffiliationcTISdnameiJ. Galvin¢kaffiliation`dnameiS. Murphyddatej“˚hfilenamegrfc1848eflags£mhiddenDefaultıiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymcpemdfullx&pem - Privacy-Enhanced Electronic Maildnamex Privacy-Enhanced Electronic Maildtypebwgbidjdoc-123884hkeywordsÑhMIME-SecdmaillmultipurposejextensionskobsoletedByÄepages0opublicationDate0n<pgranking8crfcd1848irfcNumber8estateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnamehHistoricdslugdhistfstream¢dnamedIETFdslugdietfetitlexMIME Object Security ServicesdtypecrfciupdatedByÄµhabstractyàThis document defines a framework within which security services may be applied to MIME body parts. [STANDARDS-TRACK] This memo defines a new Simple Mail Transfer Protocol (SMTP) [1] reply code, 521, which one may use to indicate that an Internet host does not accept incoming mail.  This memo defines an Experimental Protocol for the Internet community.  This memo defines an extension to the SMTP service whereby an interrupted SMTP transaction can be restarted at a later time without having to repeat all of the commands and message content sent prior to the interruption.  This memo defines an Experimental Protocol for the Internet community.darea£gacronymcsecdfullssec - Security AreadnamemSecurity AreagauthorsÑ¢kaffiliationcTISdnameiJ. Galvin¢kaffiliationiCybercashdnameiS. Murphy¢kaffiliationhInnosoftdnamejS. Crocker¢kaffiliation`dnamehN. Freedddatej“˚hfilenamegrfc1847eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymcpemdfullx&pem - Privacy-Enhanced Electronic Maildnamex Privacy-Enhanced Electronic Maildtypebwgbidjdoc-123883hkeywordsÑjMIME-EncypdmaillmultipurposejextensionskobsoletedByÄepagesopublicationDate0n<pgranking7crfcd1847irfcNumber7estateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnameqProposed Standarddslugbpsfstream¢dnamedIETFdslugdietfetitlexFSecurity Multiparts for MIME: Multipart/Signed and Multipart/EncrypteddtypecrfciupdatedByÄµhabstractxÜThis memo defines a new SMTP ([1]) reply code, 521, which one may use to indicate that an Internet host does not accept incoming mail.darea£gacronymcappdfullwapp - Applications AreadnameqApplications AreagauthorsÇ¢kaffiliationx0Institut de Mathematiques Appliquees de GrenoblednameiA. Durand¢kaffiliationx@Institut National de Recherche en Informatique et en AutomatiquednameiF. Dupontddatej”hfilenamegrfc1846eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedıegroup§gacronymgmailextdfullxmailext - Mail ExtensionsdnameoMail Extensionsdtypebwgbidjdoc-123882hkeywordsÉfsimpledmailhtransferkobsoletedByÄepagesopublicationDate0FØpgranking6crfcd1846irfcNumber6estateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnamelExperimentaldslugcexpfstream¢dnamedIETFdslugdietfetitlesSMTP 521 Reply CodedtypecrfciupdatedByÅd7504µhabstractx‹This memo defines an extension to the SMTP service whereby an interrupted SMTP transaction can be restarted 