of the issues related to network layer routing in a multi-provider Internet, and specifically to the unicast routing.  This memo provides information for the Internet community.  This memo does not specify an Internet standard of any kind.darea£gacronymcgendfullrgen - General AreadnamelGeneral AreagauthorsÅ¢kaffiliationx+T.J. Watson Research Center IBM CorporationdnamejY. Rekhterddatej—ohfilenamegrfc1787eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymdnonedfullxnone - Individual SubmissionsdnamevIndividual Submissionsdtypegindividbidjdoc-123847hkeywordsÑhInternethProtocolrArchitechure BoardcIABkobsoletedByÄepagesopublicationDate/}␀granking˚crfcd1787irfcNumber˚estateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnamemInformationaldslugcinffstream¢dnamefLegacydslugflegacyetitlex$Routing in a Multi-provider InternetdtypecrfciupdatedByÄµhabstracty(This document is an update to the original `ripe-81' proposal for representing and storing routing polices within the RIPE database.  It incorporates several extensions proposed by Merit Inc.  and gives details of a generalized IP routing policy representation to be used by all Internet routing registries.  It acts as both tutorial and provides details of database objects and attributes that use and make up a routing registry.  This memo provides information for the Internet community.  This memo does not specify an Internet standard of any kind.darea£gacronymcgendfullrgen - General AreadnamelGeneral Areagauthorsá¢kaffiliationx"MCI Telecommunications CorporationdnamehT. Bates¢kaffiliationxThe University of MichigandnameiE. Gerich¢kaffiliationdCERNdnamelL. Joncheray¢kaffiliationdRIPEdnamenJ-M. Jouanigot¢kaffiliationrBay Networks, Inc.dnamemD. Karrenberg¢kaffiliation`dnamekM. Terpstra¢kaffiliation`dnameeJ. Yuddatej Ähfilenamegrfc1786eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymdnonedfullxnone - Individual SubmissionsdnamevIndividual Submissionsdtypegindividbididoc-43296hkeywordsÄkobsoletedByÄepagesSopublicationDate/T)