 particular, this memo extends the basic Network Services Monitoring MIB to allow monitoring of Message Transfer Agents (MTAs).  It may also be used to monitor MTA components within gateways. [STANDARDS-TRACK]darea£gacronymcappdfullwapp - Applications AreadnameqApplications AreagauthorsÇ¢kaffiliationpISODE ConsortiumdnamehS. Kille¢kaffiliationxInnosoft International, Inc.dnamehN. Freedddatej“hfilenamegrfc1566eflags£mhiddenDefaultıiobsoletedıgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymfmadmandfullx&madman - Mail and Directory ManagementdnamexMail and Directory Managementdtypebwgbidjdoc-123691hkeywordsÉjManagementkInformationdBasekobsoletedByÇd2249d2789epagesopublicationDate-%-Ägrankingcrfcd1566irfcNumberestateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnameqProposed Standarddslugbpsfstream¢dnamedIETFdslugdietfetitlesMail Monitoring MIBdtypecrfciupdatedByÄµhabstractyxThis document defines a MIB which contains the elements common to the monitoring of any network service application.  This information includes a table of all monitorable network service applications, a count of the associations (connections) to each application, and basic information about the parameters and status of each application-related association. [STANDARDS-TRACK]darea£gacronymcappdfullwapp - Applications AreadnameqApplications AreagauthorsÇ¢kaffiliationpISODE ConsortiumdnamehS. Kille¢kaffiliationxInnosoft International, Inc.dnamehN. Freedddatej“hfilenamegrfc1565eflags£mhiddenDefaultıiobsoletedıgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymfmadmandfullx&madman - Mail and Directory ManagementdnamexMail and Directory Managementdtypebwgbidjdoc-123690hkeywordsÉjManagementkInformationdBasekobsoletedByÅd2248epagesopublicationDate-%-Ägrankingcrfcd1565irfcNumberestateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnameqProposed Standarddslugbpsfstream¢dnamedIETFdslugdietfetitlexNetwork Services Monitoring MIBdtypecrfciupdatedByÄµhabstracty7This document defines a set of criteria by which a DSA implementation may be judged.  Particular issues covered include conformance to standards; performance; demonstrated interoperability.  This memo provides information for the Internet community.  This memo does not specify an Internet standard of any kind.darea£gacronymcappdfullwapp - Applications AreadnameqApplications AreagauthorsÇ¢kaffiliationxUniversity College LondondnameiP. Barker¢kaffiliationxDelft Technical UniversitydnamejR. Hedbergddatej“hfilenamegrfc1564eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymeosidsdfullxosids - OSI Directory ServicesdnamevOSI Directory Servicesdtypebwgbidjdoc-123689hkeywordsÑex.500iDirectorygServiceeAgentkobsoletedByÄepagesopublicationDate-%-Ägrankingcrfcd1564irfcNumberestateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnamemInformationaldslugcinffstream¢dnamedIETFdslugdietfetitlexDSA Metrics (OSI-DS 34 (v3))dtypecrfciupdatedByÄµhabstracty4MIME [RFC-1341, RFC-1521] defines a format and general framework for the representation of a wide variety of data types in Internet mail.  This document defines one particular type of MIME data, the text/enriched type, a refinement of the "text/richtext" type defined in RFC 1341.  The text/enriched MIME type is intended to facilitate the wider interoperation of simple enriched text across a wide variety of hardware and software platforms.  This memo provides information for the Internet community.  This memo does not specify an Internet standard of any kind.darea£gacronymcgendfullrgen - General AreadnamelGeneral AreagauthorsÅ¢kaffiliationhBellcorednamemN. Borensteinddatej“hfilenamegrfc1563eflags£mhiddenDefaultıiobsoletedıgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymdnonedfullxnone - Individual SubmissionsdnamevIndividual Submissionsdtypegindividbididoc-43229hkeywordsÉeemaildmailhrichtextkobsoletedByÅd1896epagesopublicationDate-%-Ägrankingcrfcd1563irfcNumberestateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnamemInformationaldslugcinffstream¢dnamefLegacydslugflegacyetitlex#The text/enriched MIME Content-typedtypecrfciupdatedByÄµhabstractyŒThis document is an AARNet (Australian Academic and Research Network) Engineering Note (AEN-001).  AARNet Engineering Notes are engineering documents of the AARNet Engineering Working Group, and record current or proposed operational practices related to the provision of Internetworking services within Australia, and AARNet in particular.  This memo provides information for the Internet community.  This memo does not specify an Internet standard of any kind.darea£gacronymcgendfullrgen - General AreadnamelGeneral AreagauthorsÇ¢kaffiliationxThe University of QueenslanddnamemG. Michaelson¢kaffiliationxThe University of AdelaidednamehM. Priorddatej—¿hfilenamegrfc1562eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymdnonedfullxnone - Individual SubmissionsdnamevIndividual Submissionsdtypegindividbididoc-43244hkeywordsÅiAustraliakobsoletedByÄepagesopublicationDate,¸O␀grankingcrfcd1562irfcNumberestateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnamemInformationaldslugcinffstream¢dnamefLegacydslugflegacyetitlex8Naming Guidelines for the AARNet X.500 Directory ServicedtypecrfciupdatedByÄµhabstractyÆThis memo specifies a profile of the ISO/IEC 8473 Connectionless-mode Network Layer Protocol for use in conjunction with RFC 1347, TCP/UDP over Bigger Addresses.  It describes the use of CLNP to provide the lower-level service expected by Transmission Control Protocol and User Datagram Protocol.  This memo defines an Experimental Protocol for the Internet community.  This memo does not specify an Internet standard of any kind.darea£gacronymcintdfullsint - Internet AreadnamemInternet AreagauthorsÅ¢kaffiliationoCore CompetencednamemD. Piscitelloddatej—¿hfilenamegrfc1561eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymdtubadfullx+tuba - TCP/UDP Over CLNP-Addressed Networksdnamex$TCP/UDP Over CLNP-Addressed Networksdtypebwgbidjdoc-123688hkeywordsÖiCLNP-TUBAcOSIbIPhInternethProtocolkobsoletedByÄepagesopublicationDate,¸O␀grankingcrfcd1561irfcNumberestateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnamelExperimentaldslugcexpfstream¢dnamedIETFdslugdietfetitlex$Use of ISO CLNP in TUBA EnvironmentsdtypecrfciupdatedByÄµhabstractyıThere has recently been considerable discussion on two topics: MultiProtocol approaches in the Internet and the selection of a next generation Internet Protocol.  This document suggests a strawman position for goals and approaches for the IETF/IESG/IAB in these areas.  It takes the view that these two topics are related, and proposes directions for the IETF/IESG/IAB to pursue.  This memo provides information for the Internet community.  This memo does not specify an Internet standard of any kind.darea£gacronymcgendfullrgen - General AreadnamelGeneral AreagauthorsÇ¢kaffiliationx'Universities Space Research AssociationdnameiB. Leiner¢kaffiliationx&T.J. Watson Research Center, IBM Corp.dnamejY. Rekhterddatej—¿hfilenamegrfc1560eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymdnonedfullxnone - Individual SubmissionsdnamevIndividual Submissionsdtypegindividbidjdoc-123687hkeywordsÇlArchitecturehProtocolkobsoletedByÄepagesopublicationDate,¸O␀grankingcrfcd1560irfcNumberestateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnamemInformationaldslugcinffstream¢dnamefLegacydslugflegacyetitlexThe MultiProtocol InternetdtypecrfciupdatedByÄµhabstractxÀThis memo defines a set of DECnet Phase IV extensions that have been created for the Internet MIB.  It reflects changes which are the result of operational experience based on RFC 1289. [STANDARDS-TRACK]darea£gacronymcmgtdfullxmgt - Network Management AreadnamewNetwork Management AreagauthorsÅ¢kaffiliationxDigital Equipment CorporationdnamejJ. Saperiaddatej—¿hfilenamegrfc1559eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymhdecnetivdfullxdecnetiv - DECnet Phase IV MIBdnamesDECnet Phase IV MIBdtypebwgbidjdoc-123686hkeywordsÉjDECNET-MIBjManagementdSNMPkobsoletedByÄepagesEopublicationDate,¸O␀grankingcrfcd1559irfcNumberestateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnamenDraft Standarddslugbdsfstream¢dnamedIETFdslugdietfetitlexDECnet Phase IV MIB ExtensionsdtypecrfciupdatedByÄµhabstracty”The Lightweight Directory Access Protocol (LDAP) defines a network representation of a search filter transmitted to an LDAP server.  Some applications may find it useful to have a common way of representing these search filters in a human-readable form.  This document defines a human-readable string format for representing LDAP search filters.  This memo provides information for the Internet community.  This memo does not specify an Internet standard of any kind.darea£gacronymcgendfullrgen - General AreadnamelGeneral AreagauthorsÅ¢kaffiliationvUniversity of MichigandnamehT. Howesddatej—¿hfilenamegrfc1558eflags£mhiddenDefaultıiobsoletedıgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymdnonedfullxnone - Individual SubmissionsdnamevIndividual Submissionsdtypegindividbididoc-43243hkeywordsÇeX.500iDirectorykobsoletedByÅd1960epagesopublicationDate,¸O␀grankingcrfcd1558irfcNumberestateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnamemInformationaldslugcinffstream¢dnamefLegacydslugflegacyetitlex.A String Representation of LDAP Search FiltersdtypecrfciupdatedByÄµhabstractyîThis document describes the encoding method being used to represent Korean characters in both header and body part of the Internet mail messages [RFC822].  This encoding method was specified in 1991, and has since then been used.  It has now widely being used in Korean IP networks.  This memo provides information for the Internet community.  This memo does not specify an Internet standard of any kind.darea£gacronymcgendfullrgen - General AreadnamelGeneral AreagauthorsÉ¢kaffiliationx2Korea Advanced Institute of Science and TechnologydnamegU. Choi¢kaffiliationxSolvit Chosun Media, Inc.dnamegK. Chon¢kaffiliation`dnamegH. Parkddatej—øhfilenamegrfc1557eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymdnonedfullxnone - Individual SubmissionsdnamevIndividual Submissionsdtypegindividbidjdoc-123685hkeywordsÅmCharacter SetkobsoletedByÄepagesopublicationDate,¸O␀grankingcrfcd1557irfcNumberestateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnamemInforma