estateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnamemInformationaldslugcinffstream¢dnamedIRTFdslugdirtfetitlewHost Anycasting ServicedtypecrfciupdatedByÄµhabstracty¸This RFC specifies a method for assigning long addresses in the HOST- PORT specification for the data port to be used in establishing a data connection for File Transfer Protocol, FTP (STD 9, RFC 959).  This is a general solution, applicable for all "next generation" IP alternatives, and can also be extended to allow FTP operation over transport interfaces other than TCP.  This memo defines an Experimental Protocol for the Internet community.  This memo does not specify an Internet standard of any kind.darea£gacronymcgendfullrgen - General AreadnamelGeneral AreagauthorsÅ¢kaffiliationxBell Communications ResearchdnamemD. Piscitelloddatej“‘hfilenamegrfc1545eflags£mhiddenDefaultıiobsoletedıgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymdnonedfullxnone - Individual SubmissionsdnamevIndividual Submissionsdtypegindividbidjdoc-123677hkeywordsÜcFTPmFile TransferdPORTdPASVdLPRTdLPSVkobsoletedByÅd1639epagesopublicationDate,‘¬␀granking	crfcd1545irfcNumber	estateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnamelExperimentaldslugcexpfstream¢dnamefLegacydslugflegacyetitlex/FTP Operation Over Big Address Records (FOOBAR)dtypecrfciupdatedByÄµhabstractx◊This memo defines the use of an optional header field, Content-MD5, which may be used as a message integrity check (MIC), to verify that the decoded data are the same data that were initially sent. [STANDARDS-TRACK]darea£gacronymcappdfullwapp - Applications AreadnameqApplications AreagauthorsÅ¢kaffiliationxDover Beach Consulting, Inc.dnamegM. Roseddatej“”hfilenamegrfc1544eflags£mhiddenDefaultıiobsoletedıgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymf822extdfullx$822ext - Internet Message ExtensionsdnamexInternet Message Extensionsdtypebwgbidjdoc-123676hkeywordsÖdMIMEeEMailiIntegritycMICfDigestkobsoletedByÅd1864epagesopublicationDate,‘¬␀grankingcrfcd1544irfcNumberestateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnameqProposed Standarddslugbpsfstream¢dnamedIETFdslu