opublicationDate*ÛéÄgrankingacrfcd1377irfcNumberaestateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnameqProposed Standarddslugbpsfstream¢dnamedIETFdslugdietfetitlex4The PPP OSI Network Layer Control Protocol (OSINLCP)dtypecrfciupdatedByÄµhabstracty$This document defines the NCP for establishing and configuring Digital's DNA Phase IV Routing protocol (DECnet Phase IV) over PPP.  This document applies only to DNA Phase IV Routing messages (both data and control), and not to other DNA Phase IV protocols (MOP, LAT, etc.). [STANDARDS-TRACK]darea£gacronymcintdfullsint - Internet AreadnamemInternet AreagauthorsÅ¢kaffiliationoNetwork SystemsdnamehS. Senumddatej““hfilenamegrfc1376eflags£mhiddenDefaultıiobsoletedıgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymfpppextdfullx+pppext - Point-to-Point Protocol Extensionsdnamex"Point-to-Point Protocol Extensionsdtypebwgbidjdoc-123563hkeywordsÉepointcDNAeDDCMPkobsoletedByÅd1762epagesopublicationDate*ÛéÄgranking`crfcd1376irfcNumber`estateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnameqProposed Standarddslugbpsfstream¢dnamedIETFdslugdietfetitlex/The PPP DECnet Phase IV Control Protocol (DNCP)dtypecrfciupdatedByÄµhabstracty∆This RFC suggests a change in the method of specifying the IP address to add new classes of networks to be called F, G, H, and K, to reduce the amount of wasted address space, and to increase the available IP address number space, especially for smaller organizations or classes of connectors that do not need or do not want a full Class C IP address.  This memo provides information for the Internet community.  It does not specify an Internet standard.darea£gacronymcgendfullrgen - General AreadnamelGeneral AreagauthorsÅ¢kaffiliationuTansin A. Darcos, Co.dnamekP. Robinsonddatej“ˆhfilenamegrfc1375eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymdnonedfullxnone - Individual SubmissionsdnamevIndividual Submissionsdtypegindividbididoc-43183hkeywordsÇgnetworkgnumberskobsoletedByÄepagesopublicationDate* °granking_crfcd1375irfcNumber_estateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnamemInformationaldslugcinffstream¢dnamefLegacydslugflegacyetitlex*Suggestion for New Classes of IP AddressesdtypecrfciupdatedByÄµhabstracty:The ANSI X3T9.3 committee has drafted a proposal for the encapsulation of IEEE 802.2 LLC PDUs and, by implication, IP on HIPPI.  Another X3T9.3 draft describes the operation of HIPPI physical switches.  X3T9.3 chose to leave HIPPI networking issues largely outside the scope of their standards; this document discusses methods of using of ANSI standard HIPPI hardware and protocols in the context of the Internet, including the use of HIPPI switches as LANs and interoperation with other networks.  This memo is intended to become an Internet Standard. [STANDARDS-TRACK]darea£gacronymcgendfullrgen - General AreadnamelGeneral AreagauthorsÇ¢kaffiliationmCray ResearchdnamejJ. Renwick¢kaffiliation`dnamelA. NicholsonddatejÀhfilenamegrfc1374eflags£mhiddenDefaultıiobsoletedıgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymdnonedfullxnone - Individual SubmissionsdnamevIndividual Submissionsdtypegindividbidjdoc-123562hkeywordsÄkobsoletedByÅd2834epages+opublicationDate* °granking^crfcd1374irfcNumber^estateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnameqProposed Standarddslugbpsfstream¢dnamefLegacydslugflegacyetitlesIP and ARP on HIPPIdtypecrfciupdatedByÄµhabstracty¶This document comes in two parts.  The first part is for regular people who wish to set up their own DUAs (Directory User Interfaces) to access the Directory.  The second part is for ISODE-maintainers wishing to provide portable DUAs to users.  This part gives instructions in a similar but longer, step-by-step format.  This memo provides information for the Internet community.  It does not specify an Internet standard.darea£gacronymcgendfullrgen - General AreadnamelGeneral AreagauthorsÅ¢kaffiliationcISIdnameiT. Tignorddatej“ˆhfilenamegrfc1373eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymdnonedfullxnone - Individual SubmissionsdnamevIndividual Submissionsdtypegindividbididoc-43182hkeywordsäidirectoryduserfa