egacydslugflegacyetitlexInternet Activities BoarddtypecrfciupdatedByÄµhabstractx±This RFC suggests an Experimental Protocol for the Internet community.  Hosts on the Internet that choose to implement a Message Send Protocol may experiment with this protocol.darea£gacronymcgendfullrgen - General AreadnamelGeneral AreagauthorsÅ¢kaffiliation`dnameiR. Nelsonddatej !hfilenamegrfc1159eflags£mhiddenDefaultıiobsoletedıgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymdnonedfullxnone - Individual SubmissionsdnamevIndividual Submissionsdtypegindividbididoc-43078hkeywordsÄkobsoletedByÅd1312epagesopublicationDate&fpgrankingácrfcd1159irfcNumberáestateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnamelExperimentaldslugcexpfstream¢dnamefLegacydslugflegacyetitleuMessage Send ProtocoldtypecrfciupdatedByÄµhabstractyÜThis memo defines the second version of the Management Information Base (MIB-II) for use with network management protocols in TCP/IP- based internets.  In particular, together with its companion memos which describe the structure of management information (RFC 1155) along with the network management protocol (RFC 1157) for TCP/IP- based internets, these documents provide a simple, workable architecture and system for managing TCP/IP-based internets and in particular the Internet community.  This document on MIB-II incorporates all of the technical content of RFC 1156 on MIB-I and extends it, without loss of compatibilty. [STANDARDS-TRACK]darea£gacronymcgendfullrgen - General AreadnamelGeneral AreagauthorsÅ¢kaffiliation`dnameiM.T. Roseddatej ‘hfilenamegrfc1158eflags£mhiddenDefaultıiobsoletedıgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymdnonedfullxnone - Individual SubmissionsdnamevIndividual Submissionsdtypegindividbididoc-43077hkeywordsÄkobsoletedByÅd1213epagesÖopublicationDate&=3grankingÜcrfcd1158irfcNumberÜestateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnameqProposed Standarddslugbpsfstream¢dnamefLegacydslugflegacyetitlexTManagement Information Base for network management of TCP/IP-based internets: MIB-IIdtypecrfciupdatedByÄµhabstracty"This RFC is a re-release of RFC 1098, with a changed "Status of this Memo" section plus a few minor typographical corrections.  This memo defines a simple protocol by which management information for a network element may be inspected or altered by logically remote users. [STANDARDS-TRACK]darea£gacronymcgendfullrgen - General AreadnamelGeneral AreagauthorsÑ¢kaffiliation`dnameiJ.D. Case¢kaffiliation`dnamehM. Fedor¢kaffiliation`dnamepM.L. Schoffstall¢kaffiliation`dnamehJ. Davinddatej“œhfilenamegrfc1157eflags£mhiddenDefaultıiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymdnonedfullxnone - Individual SubmissionsdnamevIndividual Submissionsdtypegindividbididoc-43033hkeywordsÅdSNMPkobsoletedByÄepages$opublicationDate&=3grankingÖcrfcd1157irfcNumberÖestateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnamehHistoricdslugdhistfstream¢dnamefLegacydslugflegacyetitlex)Simple Network Management Protocol (SNMP)dtypecrfciupdatedByÄµhabstracty␀This RFC is a re-release of RFC 1066, with a changed "Status of this Memo", "IAB Policy Statement", and "Introduction" sections plus a few minor typographical corrections.  The technical content of the document is unchanged from RFC 1066. [STANDARDS-TRACK]darea£gacronymcgendfullrgen - General AreadnamelGeneral AreagauthorsÇ¢kaffiliation`dnamemK. McCloghrie¢kaffiliation`dnameiM.T. Roseddatej“œhfilenamegrfc1156eflags£mhiddenDefaultıiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymdnonedfullxnone - Individual SubmissionsdnamevIndividual Submissionsdtypegindividbididoc-43001hkeywordsÅeMIB-IkobsoletedByÄepages[opublicationDate&=3grankingÑcrfcd1156irfcNumberÑestateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnamehHistoricdslugdhistfstream¢dnamefLegacydslugflegacyetitlexLManagement Information Base for network management of TCP/IP-based internetsdtypecrfciupdatedByÄ∂habstractxÃThis RFC is a re-release of RFC 1065, with a changed "Status of this Memo", plus a few minor typographical corrections.  The technical content of the document is unchanged from RFC 1065. [STANDARDS-TRACK]darea£gacronymcgendfullrgen - Gene