mo provides information for the Internet community.  It does not specify any standard.  It is not a statement of IAB policy or recommendations. [Also FYI 2.] This catalog contains descriptions of several tools available to assist network managers in debugging and maintaining TCP/IP internets and interconnected communications resources.  Entries in the catalog tell what a tool does, how it works, and how it can be obtained.darea£gacronymcusvdfullxusv - User Services AreadnamerUser Services AreagauthorsÅ¢kaffiliation`dnamejR.H. Stineddatej»ƒhfilenamegrfc1147eflags£mhiddenDefaultıiobsoletedıgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymhnoctoolsdfulltnoctools - NOC-ToolsdnameiNOC-Toolsdtypebwgbidjdoc-123451hkeywordsÄkobsoletedByÅd1470epages±opublicationDate&µ␀granking{crfcd1147irfcNumber{estateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnamemInformationaldslugcinffstream¢dnamedIETFdslugdietfetitlexxFYI on a Network Management Tool Catalog: Tools for Monitoring and Debugging TCP/IP Internets and Interconnected DevicesdtypecrfciupdatedByÄµhabstractyThis memo is suggests a pair of TCP options to allow use of alternate data checksum algorithms in the TCP header.  The use of these options is experimental, and not recommended for production use.  Note: This RFC corrects errors introduced in the editing process in RFC 1145.darea£gacronymcgendfullrgen - General AreadnamelGeneral AreagauthorsÇ¢kaffiliation`dnamehJ. Zweig¢kaffiliation`dnamelC. Partridgeddatej“Ähfilenamegrfc1146eflags£mhiddenDefaultıiobsoletedıgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymdnonedfullxnone - Individual SubmissionsdnamevIndividual Submissionsdtypegindividbididoc-43069hkeywordsÅgTCP-ACOkobsoletedByÅd6247epagesopublicationDate%Ï÷Ägrankingzcrfcd1146irfcNumberzestateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnamehHistoricdslugdhistfstream¢dnamefLegacydslugflegacyetitlexTCP alternate checksum optionsdtypecrfciupdatedByÄµhabstractxƒThis memo is suggests a pair of TCP options to allow use of alternate data checksum algorithms in the TCP header.  The use of these options is 