resses is a proposed standard, the ideas for a general method are experimental.darea£gacronymcgendfullrgen - General AreadnamelGeneral AreagauthorsÅ¢kaffiliation`dnamenP. Mockapetrisddatej»ƒhfilenamegrfc1101eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymdnonedfullxnone - Individual SubmissionsdnamevIndividual Submissionsdtypegindividbididoc-42972hkeywordsÄkobsoletedByÄepagesopublicationDate$4ÅÄgrankingMcrfcd1101irfcNumberMestateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnamegUnknowndslugdunknfstream¢dnamefLegacydslugflegacyetitlex-DNS encoding of network names and other typesdtypecrfciupdatedByÄµhabstractyThis memo describes the state of standardization of protocols used in the Internet as determined by the Internet Activities Board (IAB).  An overview of the standards procedures is presented first, followed by discussions of the standardization process and the RFC document series, then the explanation of the terms is presented, the lists of protocols in each stage of standardization follows, and finally pointers to references and contacts for further information.  This memo is issued quarterly, please be sure the copy you are reading is dated within the last three months.  Current copies may be obtained from the Network Information Center or from the Internet Assigned Numbers Authority (see the contact information at the end of this memo).  Do not use this memo after 31-July-89.darea£gacronymcgendfullrgen - General AreadnamelGeneral AreagauthorsÇ¢kaffiliationkunspecifieddnamex)Defense Advanced Research Projects Agency¢kaffiliation`dnamexInternet Activities Boardddatej—hhfilenamegrfc1100eflags£mhiddenDefaultıiobsoletedıgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymdnonedfullxnone - Individual SubmissionsdnamevIndividual Submissionsdtypegindividbididoc-43020hkeywordsÑcIABhofficialhprotocolistandardskobsoletedByÅd1130epagesopublicationDate$4ÅÄgrankingLcrfcd1100irfcNumberLestateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnamehHistoricdslugdhistfstream¢dnamefLegacydslugflegacyetitlexIAB official protocol s