the virtual circuit facility provided by the X.25 standard of the CCITT.darea£gacronymcgendfullrgen - General AreadnamelGeneral AreagauthorsÅ¢kaffiliation`dnamejR. Ullmannddatej…zhfilenamegrfc1090eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymdnonedfullxnone - Individual SubmissionsdnamevIndividual Submissionsdtypegindividbididoc-43026hkeywordsÄkobsoletedByÄepagesopublicationDate#Êπ␀grankingBcrfcd1090irfcNumberBestateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnamegUnknowndslugdunknfstream¢dnamefLegacydslugflegacyetitlelSMTP on X.25dtypecrfciupdatedByÄµhabstracty:This memo describes an experimental method by which the Simple Network Management Protocol (SNMP) can be used over Ethernet MAC layer framing instead of the Internet UDP/IP protocol stack.  This specification is useful for LAN based network elements that support no higher layer protocols beyond the MAC sub-layer.darea£gacronymcgendfullrgen - General AreadnamelGeneral AreagauthorsÑ¢kaffiliation`dnamenM. Schoffstall¢kaffiliation`dnamehC. Davin¢kaffiliation`dnamehM. Fedor¢kaffiliation`dnamegJ. Caseddatej…zhfilenamegrfc1089eflags£mhiddenDefaultıiobsoletedıgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymdnonedfullxnone - Individual SubmissionsdnamevIndividual Submissionsdtypegindividbididoc-43025hkeywordsÄkobsoletedByÅd4789epagesopublicationDate#Êπ␀grankingAcrfcd1089irfcNumberAestateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnamegUnknowndslugdunknfstream¢dnamefLegacydslugflegacyetitlerSNMP over EthernetdtypecrfciupdatedByÄ∂habstractxtThis document specifies a standard method of encapsulating the Internet Protocol (IP) datagrams on NetBIOS networks.darea£gacronymcgendfullrgen - General AreadnamelGeneral AreagauthorsÅ¢kaffiliation`dnameoL.J. McLaughlinddatej—‚hfilenamegrfc1088eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymdnonedfullxnone - Individual SubmissionsdnamevIndividual Submissionsdtypegindividbididoc-43024hkeywordsÅjIP-NETBIOSkobsoletedByÄepagesopublicationDate#Êπ␀granking@crfcd1088irfcNumber@estateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnameqInternet Standarddslugcstdfstream¢dnamefLegacydslugflegacyisubseries£gacronymcstdfnumber0etotaletitlexCStandard for the transmission of IP datagrams over NetBIOS networksdtypecrfciupdatedByÄµhabstractxÖThis memo is a statement of policy by the Internet Activities Board (IAB) concerning the proper use of the resources of the Internet.darea£gacronymcgendfullrgen - General AreadnamelGeneral AreagauthorsÇ¢kaffiliationkunspecifieddnamex)Defense Advanced Research Projects Agency¢kaffiliation`dnamexInternet Activities Boardddatej“hfilenamegrfc1087eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymdnonedfullxnone - Individual SubmissionsdnamevIndividual Submissionsdtypegindividbididoc-43023hkeywordsÇfEthicshInternetkobsoletedByÄepagesopublicationDate#Ω⁄Ägranking?crfcd1087irfcNumber?estateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnamegUnknowndslugdunknfstream¢dnamefLegacydslugflegacyetitlewEthics and the InternetdtypecrfciupdatedByÄµhabstractyThis memo proposes a standard for the Internet community.  Hosts on the Internet that choose to implement ISO TP0 transport connectivity between TCP and X.25 based hosts are expected to experiment with this proposal.  TCP port 146 is reserved for this proposal.darea£gacronymcgendfullrgen - General AreadnamelGeneral AreagauthorsÇ¢kaffiliation`dnamekJ.P. Onions¢kaffiliation`dnameiM.T. Roseddatej…Bhfilenamegrfc1086eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymdnonedfullxnone - Individual SubmissionsdnamevIndividual Submissionsdtypegindividbididoc-43022hkeywordsÄkobsoletedByÄepages	opublicationDate#î¸␀granking>crfcd1086irfcNumber>estateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnamegUnknowndslugdunknfstream¢dnamefLegacydslugflegacyetitlex#ISO-TP0 bridge between TCP and X.25dtypecrfciupdatedByÄµhabstracty^RFC 1006 describes a mechanism for providing the ISO transport service on top of TCP/IP.  Once this method is applied, one may implement "real" ISO applications on top of TCP/IP-based internets, by simply implementing OSI session, presentation, and application services on top of the transport service access point which is provided on top of the TCP.  Although straight-forward, there are some environments in which the richness provided by the OSI application layer is desired, but it is nonetheless impractical to implement the underlying OSI infrastructure (i.e., the presentation, session, and transport services on top of the TCP).  This memo describes an approach for providing "stream-lined" support of OSI application services on top of TCP/IP-based internets for such constrained environments.  This memo proposes a standard for the Internet community.darea£gacronymcgendfullrgen - General AreadnamelGeneral AreagauthorsÅ¢kaffiliation`dnameiM.T. Roseddatej…Ahfilenamegrfc1085eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymdnonedfullxnone - Individual SubmissionsdnamevIndividual Submissionsdtypegindividbididoc-43021hkeywordsÄkobsoletedByÄepages opublicationDate#î¸␀granking=crfcd1085irfcNumber=estateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnamegUnknowndslugdunknfstream¢dnamefLegacydslugflegacyetitlex:ISO presentation services on top of TCP/IP based internetsdtypecrfciupdatedByÄµhabstractx¯This RFC is a slight revision and extension of RFC-1048 by Philip Prindeville.  This memo will be updated as additional tags are are defined.  This edition introduces Tag 13 for Boot File Size.  Comments and suggestions for improvements are sought.darea£gacronymcgendfullrgen - General AreadnamelGeneral AreagauthorsÅ¢kaffiliationcISIdnamemJ.K. Reynoldsddatej…Ahfilenamegrfc1084eflags£mhiddenDefaultıiobsoletedıgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymdnonedfullxnone - Individual SubmissionsdnamevIndividual Submissionsdtypegindividbididoc-42983hkeywordsÄkobsoletedByÉd1533d1395d1497epagesopublicationDate#î¸␀granking<crfcd1084irfcNumber<estateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnamegUnknowndslugdunknfstream¢dnamefLegacydslugflegacyetitlex#BOOTP vendor information extensionsdtypecrfciupdatedByÄµhabstractyBThis memo describes the state of standardization of protocols used in the Internet as determined by the Internet Activities Board (IAB).  An overview of the standards procedures is presented first, followed by discussions of the standardization process and the RFC document series, then the explanation of the terms is presented, the lists of protocols in each stage of standardization follows, and finally pointers to references and contacts for further information.  This memo is issued quarterly, please be sure the copy you are reading is dated within the last three months.darea£gacronymcgendfullrgen - General AreadnamelGeneral AreagauthorsÅ¢kaffiliationkunspecifieddnamexInternet Activities Boardddatej—ºhfilenamegrfc1083eflags£mhiddenDefaultıiobsoletedıgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymdnonedfullxnone - Individual SubmissionsdnamevIndividual Submissionsdtypegindividbididoc-43019hkeywordsÑcIABhofficialhprotocolistandardskobsoletedByÅd1100epagesopublicationDate#î¸␀granking;crfcd1083irfcNumber;estateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnamehHistoricdslugdhistfstream¢dnamefLegacydslugflegacyetitlexIAB official protocol standardsdtypecrfciupdatedByÄµhabstractyÃThis memo suggests a simple method for workstations to dynamically access mail from a discussion group server, as an extension to an earlier memo which dealt with dynamically accessing mail from a mailbox server using the Post Office Protocol - Version 3 (POP3).  This RFC specifies a proposed protocol for the Internet community, and requests discussion and suggestions for improvements.  All of the extensions described in this memo to the POP3 are OPTIONAL.darea£gacronymcgendfullrgen - General AreadnamelGeneral AreagauthorsÅ¢kaffiliation`dnameiM.T. Roseddatej ›hfilenamegrfc1082eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymdnonedfullxnone - Individual SubmissionsdnamevIndividual Submissionsdtypegindividbididoc-43018hkeywordsÄkobsoletedByÄepagesopublicationDate#mo␀granking:crfcd1082irfcNumber:estateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnamegUnknowndslugdunknfstream¢dnamefLegacydslugflegacye