FC 1024 contains detailed assignments of numbers and structures used in this system.  Portions of RFC 1024 that define query language structures are superceded by definitions in this memo.  This memo assumes a knowledge of the ISO data encoding standard, ASN.1.darea£gacronymcgendfullrgen - General AreadnamelGeneral AreagauthorsÇ¢kaffiliation`dnamejG. Trewitt¢kaffiliation`dnamelC. Partridgeddatej ›hfilenamegrfc1076eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymdnonedfullxnone - Individual SubmissionsdnamevIndividual Submissionsdtypegindividbididoc-42962hkeywordsÄkobsoletedByÄepages*opublicationDate#mo␀granking4crfcd1076irfcNumber4estateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnamegUnknowndslugdunknfstream¢dnamefLegacydslugflegacyetitlex$HEMS monitoring and control languagedtypecrfciupdatedByÄµhabstracty=This RFC describes a distance-vector-style routing protocol for routing multicast datagrams through an internet.  It is derived from the Routing Information Protocol (RIP), and implements multicasting as described in RFC-1054.  This is an experimental protocol, and its implementation is not recommended at this time.darea£gacronymcgendfullrgen - General AreadnamelGeneral AreagauthorsÉ¢kaffiliation`dnamekD. Waitzman¢kaffiliation`dnamelC. Partridge¢kaffiliation`dnamelS.E. Deeringddatej“—hfilenamegrfc1075eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymdnonedfullxnone - Individual SubmissionsdnamevIndividual Submissionsdtypegindividbididoc-43011hkeywordsÅhIP-DVMRPkobsoletedByÄepagesopublicationDate#mo␀granking3crfcd1075irfcNumber3estateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnamelExperimentaldslugcexpfstream¢dnamefLegacydslugflegacyetitlex*Distance Vector Multicast Routing ProtocoldtypecrfciupdatedByÄµhabstractxàThis RFC is an implementation description of the standard ANSI IS-IS and ISO ES-IS routing protocols within the NSFNET backbone network.darea£gacronymcgendfullrgen - General AreadnamelGeneral AreagauthorsÅ¢kaffiliation`dnamejJ. RekhterddatejÀhfilenamegrfc1074eflag