ternet checksum.  It is not a standard, but a set of useful implementation techniques.darea£gacronymcgendfullrgen - General AreadnamelGeneral AreagauthorsÉ¢kaffiliation`dnamekR.T. Braden¢kaffiliation`dnamekD.A. Borman¢kaffiliation`dnamelC. PartridgeddatejÀFhfilenamegrfc1071eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedıegroup§gacronymdnonedfullxnone - Individual SubmissionsdnamevIndividual Submissionsdtypegindividbididoc-43006hkeywordsÄkobsoletedByÄepagesopublicationDate#ıpgranking/crfcd1071irfcNumber/estateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnamemInformationaldslugcinffstream¢dnamefLegacydslugflegacyetitlexComputing the Internet checksumdtypecrfciupdatedByÅd1141µhabstractyªThis RFC proposes a scenario for experimentation with the International Organization for Standardization (ISO) Open Systems Interconnection (OSI) network layer protocols over the Internet and requests discussion and suggestions for improvements to this scenario.  This RFC also proposes the creation of an experimental OSI internet.  To participate in the experimental OSI internet, a system must abide by the agreements set forth in this RFC.darea£gacronymcgendfullrgen - General AreadnamelGeneral AreagauthorsÉ¢kaffiliation`dnamekR.A. Hagens¢kaffiliation`dnameiN.E. Hall¢kaffiliation`dnameiM.T. Roseddatej…yhfilenamegrfc1070eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymdnonedfullxnone - Individual SubmissionsdnamevIndividual Submissionsdtypegindividbididoc-43005hkeywordsÄkobsoletedByÄepagesopublicationDate#Êπ␀granking.crfcd1070irfcNumber.estateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnamegUnknowndslugdunknfstream¢dnamefLegacydslugflegacyetitlexRUse of the Internet as a subnetwork for experimentation with the OSI network layerdtypecrfciupdatedByÄµhabstractytThis RFC suggests an addressing scheme for use with the ISO Connectionless Network Protocol (CLNP) in the Internet.  This is a solution to one of the problems inherent in the use of "ISO-grams" in the Internet.  This memo is a revision of RFC 986.  This RFC suggests a proposed protocol for the Internet community, and requests discussion and suggestions for improvements.darea£gacronymcgendfullrgen - General AreadnamelGeneral AreagauthorsÇ¢kaffiliation`dnameiR. Callon¢kaffiliation`dnamejH.W. Braunddatej…yhfilenamegrfc1069eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymdnonedfullxnone - Individual SubmissionsdnamevIndividual Submissionsdtypegindividbididoc-42923hkeywordsÄkobsoletedByÄepages
opublicationDate#Êπ␀granking-crfcd1069irfcNumber-estateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnamegUnknowndslugdunknfstream¢dnamefLegacydslugflegacyetitlex_Guidelines for the use of Internet-IP addresses in the ISO Connectionless-Mode Network ProtocoldtypecrfciupdatedByÄµhabstractxÓThis RFC describes an Internet background file transfer service that is built upon the third-party transfer model of FTP.  No new protocols are involved.  The purpose of this memo is to stimulate discussions on new Internet service modes.darea£gacronymcgendfullrgen - General AreadnamelGeneral AreagauthorsÇ¢kaffiliation`dnamelA.L. DeSchon¢kaffiliation`dnamekR.T. Bradenddatej—Khfilenamegrfc1068eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymdnonedfullxnone - Individual SubmissionsdnamevIndividual Submissionsdtypegindividbididoc-43004hkeywordsÅcFTPkobsoletedByÄepagesopublicationDate"Ùgranking,crfcd1068irfcNumber,estateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnamegUnknowndslugdunknfstream¢dnamefLegacydslugflegacyetitlex'Background File Transfer Program (BFTP)dtypecrfciupdatedByÄµhabstractysThis RFC defines a simple protocol by which management information for a network element may be inspected or altered by logically remote users.  In particular, together with its companion memos which describe the structure of management information along with the initial management information base, these documents provide a simple, workable architecture and system for managing TCP/IP-based internets and in particular, the Internet.  This memo specifies a draft standard for the Internet community.  TCP/IP implementations in the Internet which are network manageable are expected to adopt and implement this specification.darea£gacronymcgendfullrgen - General AreadnamelGeneral AreagauthorsÑ¢kaffiliation`dnameiJ.D. Case¢kaffiliation`dnamehM. Fedor¢kaffiliation`dnamepM.L. Schoffstall¢kaffiliation`dnamehJ. Davinddatej»ñhfilenamegrfc1067eflags£mhiddenDefaultıiobsoletedıgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymdnonedfullxnone - Individual SubmissionsdnamevIndividual Submissionsdtypegindividbididoc-43002hkeywordsÄkobsoletedByÅd1098epages!opublicationDate"Ùgranking+crfcd1067irfcNumber+estateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnamegUnknowndslugdunknfstream¢dnamefLegacydslugflegacyetitlex"Simple Network Management ProtocoldtypecrfciupdatedByÄµhabstractyäThis RFC provides the initial version of the Management Information Base (MIB) for use with network management protocols in TCP/IP-based internets in the short-term.  In particular, together with its companion memos which describe the structure of management information along with the initial network management protocol, these documents provide a simple, workable architecture and system for managing TCP/IP-based internets, and in particular, the Internet.  This memo specifies a draft standard for the Internet community.  TCP/IP implementations in the Internet which are network manageable are expected to adopt and implement this specification.darea£gacronymcgendfullrgen - General AreadnamelGeneral AreagauthorsÇ¢kaffiliation`dnamemK. McCloghrie¢kaffiliation`dnameiM.T. Roseddatej»ˇhfilenamegrfc1066eflags£mhiddenDefaultıiobsoletedıgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymdnonedfullxnone - Individual SubmissionsdnamevIndividual Submissionsdtypegindividbididoc-43000hkeywordsÄkobsoletedByÅd1156epagesZopublicationDate"Ùgranking*crfcd1066irfcNumber*estateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnamegUnknowndslugdunknfstream¢dnamefLegacydslugflegacyetitlexLManagement Information Base for network management of TCP/IP-based internetsdtypecrfciupdatedByÄµhabstractyfThis RFC provides the common definitions for the structure and identification of management information for TCP/IP-based internets.  In particular, together with its companion memos, which describe the initial management information base along with the initial network management protocol, these documents provide a simple, working architecture and system for managing TCP/IP-based internets and in particular, the Internet.  This memo specifies a draft standard for the Internet community.  TCP/IP implementation in the Internet which are network manageable are expected to adopt and implement this specification.darea£gacronymcgendfullrgen - General AreadnamelGeneral AreagauthorsÇ¢kaffiliation`dnamemK. McCloghrie¢kaffiliation`dnameiM.T. Roseddatej»ˇhfilenamegrfc1065eflags£mhiddenDefaultıiobsoletedıgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymdnonedfullxnone - Individual SubmissionsdnamevIndividual Submissionsdtypegindividbididoc-42998hkeywordsÄkobsoletedByÅd1155epagesopublicationDate"Ùgranking)crfcd1065irfcNumber)estateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnameqInternet Standarddslugcstdfstream¢dnamefLegacydslugflegacyetitlexQStructure and identification of management information for TCP/IP-based internetsdtypecrfciupdatedByÄµhabstracty%This memo suggests a method for workstations to dynamically access mail from a mailbox server ("respository").  This RFC specifies a standard for the SUMEX-AIM community and a proposed experimental protocol for the Internet community.  Discussion and suggestions for improvement are requested.darea£gacronymcgendfullrgen - General AreadnamelGeneral AreagauthorsÅ¢kaffiliation`dnamelM.R. Crispinddatej…Ìhfilenamegrfc1064eflags£mhiddenDefaultıiobsoletedıgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymdnonedfullxnone - Individual SubmissionsdnamevIndividual Submissionsdtypegindividbididoc-42995hkeywordsÄkobsoletedByÇd1176d1203epagesopublicationDate"À8pgranking(crfcd1064irfcNumber(estateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnamegUnknowndslugdunknfstream¢dnamefLegacydslugflegacyetitlex+Interactive Mail Access Protocol: Version 2dtypecrfciupdatedByÄµhabstractx∫A pair of IP options that can be used to learn the minimum MTU of a path through an internet is described, along with its possible uses.  This is a proposal for an Experimental protocol.darea£gacronymcgendfullrgen - General AreadnamelGeneral AreagauthorsÑ¢kaffiliation`dnamejJ.C. Mogul¢kaffiliation`dnameiC.A. Kent¢kaffiliation`dnamelC. Partridge¢kaffiliation`dnamemK. McCloghrieddatej…Ìhfilenamegrfc1063eflags£mhiddenDefaultıiobsoletedıgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymdnonedfullxnone - Individual SubmissionsdnamevIndividual Submissionsdtypegindividbididoc-42993hkeywordsÄkobsoletedByÅd1191epagesopublicationDate"À8pgranking'crfcd1063irfcNumber'estateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnamegUnknowndslugdunknfstream¢dnamefLegacydslugflegacyetitlexIP MTU discovery optionsdtypecrfciupdatedByÄµhabstractxÉThis memo is an official status report on the network numbers and gateway autonomous system numbers used in the Internet community.darea£gacronymcgendfullrgen - General AreadnamelGeneral AreagauthorsÉ¢kaffiliation`dnameiS. Romano¢kaffiliation`dnamejM.K. Stahl¢kaffiliation`dnameiM. Reckerddatej»ˇhfilenamegrfc1062eflags£mhiddenDefaultıiobsoletedıgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymdnonedfullxnone - Individual SubmissionsdnamevIndividual Submissionsdtypegindividbididoc-42957hkeywordsÄkobsoletedByÇd1117d1166epagesAopublicationDate"Ùgranking&crfcd1062irfcNumber&estateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnamegUnknowndslugdunknfstream¢dnamefLegacydslugflegacyetitlepInternet numbersdtypecrfciupdatedByÄµhabstractx°This memo is a status report on the parameters (i.e., numbers and keywords) used in protocols in the Internet community.  Distribution of this memo is unlimited.darea£gacronymcgendfullrgen - General AreadnamelGeneral AreagauthorsÇ¢kaffiliation`dnamemJ.K. Reynolds¢kaffiliation`dnameiJ. Postelddatej chfilenamegrfc1060eflags£mhiddenDefaultıiobsoletedıgupdatedıegroup§gacronymdnonedfullxnone - Individual SubmissionsdnamevIndividual Submissionsdtypegindividbididoc-42948hkeywordsÄkobsoletedByÅd1340epagesVopublicationDate%Ï÷Ägranking$crfcd1060irfcNumber$estateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnamehHistoricdslugdhistfstream¢dnamefLegacydslugflegacyetitlepAssigned numbersdtypecrfciupdatedByÅd1349µhabstracty∆This memo describes the Network Time Protocol (NTP), specifies its formal structure and summarizes information useful for its implementation.  NTP provides the mechanisms to synchronize time and coordinate time distribution in a large, diverse internet operating at rates from mundane to lightwave.  It uses a returnable-time design in which a distributed subnet of time servers operating in a self- organizing, hierarchical master-slave configuration synchronizes logical clocks within the subnet and to national time standards via wire or radio.  The servers can also redistribute reference time via local routing algorithms and time daemons.  The NTP architectures, algorithms and protocols which have evolved over several years of implementation and refinement are described in this document.  The prototype system, which has been in regular operation in the Internet for the last two years, is described in an Appendix along with performance data which shows that timekeeping accuracy throughout most portions of the Internet can be ordinarily maintained to within a few tens of milliseconds, even the cases of failure or disruption of clocks, time servers or nets.  This is a Draft Standard for an Elective protocol.darea£gacronymcgendfullrgen - General AreadnamelGeneral AreagauthorsÅ¢kaffiliation`dnamejD.L. Millsddatej“4hfilenamegrfc1059eflags£mhiddenDefaultıiobsoletedıgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymdnonedfullxnone - Individual SubmissionsdnamevIndividual Submissionsdtypegindividbididoc-42890hkeywordsÖcNTPeNTPv1dtimeeclockosynchronizationkobsoletedByÇd1119d1305epages:opublicationDate"À8pgranking#crfcd1059irfcNumber#estateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnamegUnknowndslugdunknfstream¢dnamefLegacydslugflegacyetitlexBNetwork Time Protocol (version 1) specification and implementationdtypecrfciupdatedByÄµhabstractx”This RFC describes an existing protocol for exchanging routing information among gateways and other hosts.  It is intended to be used as a basis for developing gateway software for use in the Internet community.darea£gacronymcgendfullrgen - General AreadnamelGeneral AreagauthorsÅ¢kaffiliation`dnamelC.L. Hedrickddatej“Shfilenamegrfc1058eflags£mhiddenDefaultıiobsoletedÙgupdatedı