This RFC specifies a standard for the ARPA Internet community.  Hosts on the ARPA Internet that choose to implement a Echo Protocol are expected to adopt and implement this standard.  The Echo service simply sends back to the originating source any data it receives.darea£gacronymcgendfullrgen - General AreadnamelGeneral AreagauthorsÅ¢kaffiliationcISIdnameiJ. Postelddatej“Œhfilenamefrfc862eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymdnonedfullxnone - Individual SubmissionsdnamevIndividual Submissionsdtypegindividbididoc-42787hkeywordsÅdECHOkobsoletedByÄepagesopublicationDate(pgranking^crfcc862irfcNumber^estateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnameqInternet Standarddslugcstdfstream¢dnamefLegacydslugflegacyisubseries£gacronymcstdfnumberetotaletitlemEcho ProtocoldtypecrfciupdatedByÄ∂habstractx˜This Telnet Option provides a mechanism for extending the set of possible options.  This RFC specifies a standard for the ARPA Internet community.  Hosts on the ARPA Internet are expected to adopt and implement this standard.  Obsoletes NIC 16239.darea£gacronymcgendfullrgen - General AreadnamelGeneral AreagauthorsÇ¢kaffiliationcISIdnameiJ. Postel¢kaffiliation`dnamekJ. Reynoldsddatej“Œhfilenamefrfc861eflags£mhiddenDefaultÙiobsoletedÙgupdatedÙegroup§gacronymdnonedfullxnone - Individual SubmissionsdnamevIndividual Submissionsdtypegindividbididoc-42786hkeywordsÅjTOPT-EXTOPkobsoletedByÄepagesopublicationDate(pgranking]crfcc861irfcNumber]estateÅiPublishedfstatus¢dnameqInternet Standarddslugcstdfstream¢dnamefLegacydslugflegacyisubseries£gacronymcstdfnumber etotaletitlex$Telnet Extended Options: List OptiondtypecrfciupdatedByÄ∂habstractx˛This Telnet Option provides a way to check the roundtrip path between two Telnet modules.  This RFC specifies a standard for the ARPA Internet community.  Hosts on the ARPA Internet are expected to adopt and implement this standard.  Obsoletes NIC 16238.darea£gacronymcgendfullrgen - General AreadnamelGeneral AreagauthorsÇ¢kaffiliat